| C053 | 4.18.0→4.18.1 | パッチ | 高 | オプション/クラス/API名・形式の変更 | camel-yaml-io, camel-xml-io | camel-yaml-io / camel-xml-io | 旧名称(オプション名・クラス名・ヘッダー名・XML/YAML属性)を grep し、新名称へ置換。XML/YAML DSL は属性形式の変更もあるため route ファイルも対象 | camel-yaml-io, camel-xml-io, routePolicy, routePolicyRef, route, <compensation>, <completion>, <saga>, uri, completion, compensation | In the YAML DSL we have renamed `routePolicy` to `routePolicyRef` on the `route` node, as that is the correct name. The Saga EIP has _fixed_ the model for how to configure completion and compensation URIs. For Java DSL there is no changes, but XML and YAML DSL is affected. Here the `<compensation>` and `<completion>` tags has been changed to be an attribute on `<saga>` instead as shown below: Before: In YAML DSL the changes are even simpler as the endpoint is moved from `uri` to the value of `co | あり | In the YAML DSL we have renamed `routePolicy` to `routePolicyRef` on the `route` node,<br>as that is the correct name.<br><br>## Saga EIP<br><br>The Saga EIP has _fixed_ the model for how to configure completion and compensation URIs.<br><br>For Java DSL there is no changes, but XML and YAML DSL is affected. Here the `<compensation>` and `<completion>` tags<br>has been changed to be an attribute on `<saga>` instead as shown below:<br><br>Before:<br><br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <route><br>        <from uri="direct:start"/><br>        <saga sagaService="mySagaService"><br>            <compensation uri="mock:compensation"/><br>            <completion uri="mock:completion"/><br>            <option key="myOptionKey"><br>                <constant>myOptionValue</constant><br>            </option><br>            <option key="myOptionKey2"><br>                <constant>myOptionValue2</constant><br>            </option><br>        </saga><br>        <choice><br>            <when><br>                <simple>${body} == 'fail'</simple><br>                <throwException exceptionType="java.lang.RuntimeException" message="fail"/><br>            </when><br>        </choice><br>        <to uri="mock:end"/><br>    </route><br><br>In YAML DSL the changes are even simpler as the endpoint is moved from `uri` to the value of `completion` or `compensation`.<br><br>[source,yaml]<br>[code]<br>    - route:<br>        from:<br>          uri: direct:start<br>          steps:<br>            - saga:<br>                sagaService: mySagaService<br>                compensation:<br>                  uri: mock:compensation<br>                completion:<br>                  uri: mock:completion<br>                option:<br>                  - key: myOptionKey<br>                    expression:<br>                      constant:<br>                        expression: myOptionValue<br>                  - key: myOptionKey2<br>                    expression:<br>                      constant:<br>                        expression: myOptionValue2<br>            - choice:<br>                when:<br>                  - expression:<br>                      simple:<br>                        expression: "${body} == 'fail'"<br>                    steps:<br>                      - throwException:<br>                          message: fail<br>                          exceptionType: java.lang.RuntimeException<br>            - to:<br>                uri: mock:end<br>    <br><br>After:<br><br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <route><br>        <from uri="direct:start"/><br>        <saga sagaService="mySagaService" compensation="mock:compensation" completion="mock:completion"><br>            <option key="myOptionKey"><br>                <constant>myOptionValue</constant><br>            </option><br>            <option key="myOptionKey2"><br>                <constant>myOptionValue2</constant><br>            </option><br>        </saga><br>        <choice><br>            <when><br>                <simple>${body} == 'fail'</simple><br>                <throwException exceptionType="java.lang.RuntimeException" message="fail"/><br>            </when><br>        </choice><br>        <to uri="mock:end"/><br>    </route><br><br>[source,yaml]<br>[code]<br>    - route:<br>        from:<br>          uri: direct:start<br>          steps:<br>            - saga:<br>                sagaService: mySagaService<br>                compensation: mock:compensation<br>                completion: mock:completion<br>                option:<br>                  - key: myOptionKey<br>                    expression:<br>                      constant:<br>                        expression: myOptionValue<br>                  - key: myOptionKey2<br>                    expression:<br>                      constant:<br>                        expression: myOptionValue2<br>            - choice:<br>                when:<br>                  - expression:<br>                      simple:<br>                        expression: "${body} == 'fail'"<br>                    steps:<br>                      - throwException:<br>                          message: fail<br>                          exceptionType: java.lang.RuntimeException<br>            - to:<br>                uri: mock:end | 未調査 |  |
| C054 | 4.18.0→4.18.1 | パッチ | 高 | オプション/クラス/API名・形式の変更 | camel-simple | camel-simple | 旧名称(オプション名・クラス名・ヘッダー名・XML/YAML属性)を grep し、新名称へ置換。XML/YAML DSL は属性形式の変更もあるため route ファイルも対象 | camel-simple | In the simple language then init blocks syntax has changed to require that each variable ends with a semicolon and new line (no trailing comments etc is allowed) For example Should be changed to have semicolons as shown below: | あり | In the simple language then init blocks syntax has changed to require that each variable ends with a semicolon and new line (no trailing comments etc is allowed)<br><br>For example<br><br>[source,yaml]<br>[code]<br>        - setBody:<br>            simple:<br>              expression: \|-<br>                $init{<br>                  // this is a java like comment<br>                  $sum := ${sum(${header.lines},100)}<br>    <br>                  $sku := ${iif(${body} contains 'Camel',123,999)}<br>                }init$<br>                orderId=$sku,total=$sum<br><br>Should be changed to have semicolons as shown below:<br><br>[source,yaml]<br>[code]<br>        - setBody:<br>            simple:<br>              expression: \|-<br>                $init{<br>                  // this is a java like comment<br>                  $sum := ${sum(${header.lines},100)};<br>    <br>                  $sku := ${iif(${body} contains 'Camel',123,999)};<br>                }init$<br>                orderId=$sku,total=$sum | 未調査 |  |
| C055 | 4.18.0→4.18.1 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-mail | camel-mail | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-mail, IdempotentRepository, camel-mail, camel-file | When configured a custom `IdempotentRepository` on `camel-mail` endpoint, then Camel will now auto-start the bean which is similar to what `camel-file` do as well. | あり | When configured a custom `IdempotentRepository` on `camel-mail` endpoint, then Camel will now auto-start<br>the bean which is similar to what `camel-file` do as well. | 未調査 |  |
| C056 | 4.18.0→4.18.1 | パッチ | 中 | 非推奨 | camel-json-patch | camel-json-patch | 使用有無を grep。今回の更新では動く想定だが、次回以降の削除に備えて代替先を確認 | camel-json-patch, camel-json-patch | The `camel-json-patch` is now deprecated - the library it uses is not active maintained and this module does not work with Jackon 3. | あり | The `camel-json-patch` is now deprecated - the library it uses is not active maintained and this module does not work with Jackon 3. | 未調査 |  |
| C057 | 4.18.0→4.18.1 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-openapi-java | camel-openapi-java | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-openapi-java, base.path, base.path=cheese | When using _code first_ Rest DSL and have configured `base.path` then this will now be exclusively used for the returned server url in the API specification. For example here we set `base.path=cheese`: Then the generated API specification now returns: Previously the context-path would always be used: The intention is to allow to configure the `base.path` _as is_ in the return API specification. | あり | When using _code first_ Rest DSL and have configured `base.path` then this will now be exclusively used<br>for the returned server url in the API specification.<br><br>For example here we set `base.path=cheese`:<br><br>[source,java]<br>[code]<br>    restConfiguration().component("jetty").host("localhost").port(getPort())<br>            .contextPath("myapp")<br>            .apiContextPath("/api-doc")<br>            .apiProperty("cors", "true").apiProperty("base.path", "cheese")<br>            .apiProperty("api.title", "The hello rest thing").apiProperty("api.version", "1.2.3");<br><br>Then the generated API specification now returns:<br><br>[source,json]<br>[code]<br>      "servers" : [ {<br>        "url" : "http://localhost:58678/cheese"<br>      } ],<br><br>Previously the context-path would always be used:<br><br>[source,json]<br>[code]<br>      "servers" : [ {<br>        "url" : "http://localhost:58678/myapp"<br>      } ],<br><br>The intention is to allow to configure the `base.path` _as is_ in the return API specification. | 未調査 |  |
| C058 | 4.18.1→4.18.3 | パッチ | 高 | 破壊的変更(要確認) | camel-jackson | camel-jackson - potential breaking change | 原文全文を読み、該当するオプション/クラス/ヘッダー/URI を grep。使用していれば修正が必要 | camel-jackson, camel-jackson, ObjectMapper, MapperFeature.BLOCK_UNSAFE_POLYMORPHIC_BASE_TYPES, Object, Serializable, Comparable, objectMapper | The `camel-jackson` data format now creates its default `ObjectMapper` with `MapperFeature.BLOCK_UNSAFE_POLYMORPHIC_BASE_TYPES` enabled, consistent with the mapper used by the component's JSON data-type transformer. This is defense-in-depth against gadget-chain deserialization: when polymorphic / default typing is enabled, Jackson refuses unsafe base types (such as `Object`, `Serializable` or `Comparable`). This only affects routes that enable polymorphic / default typing on an unsafe base type; | あり | The `camel-jackson` data format now creates its default `ObjectMapper` with<br>`MapperFeature.BLOCK_UNSAFE_POLYMORPHIC_BASE_TYPES` enabled, consistent with the mapper used by the<br>component's JSON data-type transformer. This is defense-in-depth against gadget-chain deserialization: when<br>polymorphic / default typing is enabled, Jackson refuses unsafe base types (such as `Object`, `Serializable`<br>or `Comparable`).<br><br>This only affects routes that enable polymorphic / default typing on an unsafe base type; ordinary<br>marshalling and unmarshalling are unchanged. If you rely on that behaviour, supply your own `ObjectMapper`<br>(via the `objectMapper` option or the registry) configured without this feature. | 未調査 |  |
| C059 | 4.18.1→4.18.3 | パッチ | 高 | 破壊的変更(要確認) | camel-jacksonxml | camel-jacksonxml - potential breaking change | 原文全文を読み、該当するオプション/クラス/ヘッダー/URI を grep。使用していれば修正が必要 | camel-jacksonxml, camel-jacksonxml, XmlMapper, MapperFeature.BLOCK_UNSAFE_POLYMORPHIC_BASE_TYPES, camel-jackson, Object, Serializable, Comparable, xmlMapper | The `camel-jacksonxml` data format now creates its default `XmlMapper` with `MapperFeature.BLOCK_UNSAFE_POLYMORPHIC_BASE_TYPES` enabled, mirroring the same hardening applied to `camel-jackson`. This is defense-in-depth against gadget-chain deserialization: when polymorphic / default typing is enabled, Jackson refuses unsafe base types (such as `Object`, `Serializable` or `Comparable`). This only affects routes that enable polymorphic / default typing on an unsafe base type; ordinary marshalling | あり | The `camel-jacksonxml` data format now creates its default `XmlMapper` with<br>`MapperFeature.BLOCK_UNSAFE_POLYMORPHIC_BASE_TYPES` enabled, mirroring the same hardening applied to<br>`camel-jackson`. This is defense-in-depth against gadget-chain deserialization: when polymorphic / default<br>typing is enabled, Jackson refuses unsafe base types (such as `Object`, `Serializable` or `Comparable`).<br><br>This only affects routes that enable polymorphic / default typing on an unsafe base type; ordinary<br>marshalling and unmarshalling are unchanged. If you rely on that behaviour, supply your own `XmlMapper`<br>(via the `xmlMapper` option) configured without this feature. | 未調査 |  |
| C060 | 4.18.1→4.18.3 | パッチ | 高 | 破壊的変更(要確認) | camel-jackson-avro, camel-jackson-protobuf | camel-jackson-avro and camel-jackson-protobuf - potential breaking change | 原文全文を読み、該当するオプション/クラス/ヘッダー/URI を grep。使用していれば修正が必要 | camel-jackson-avro, camel-jackson-protobuf, camel-jackson-avro, camel-jackson-protobuf, AvroMapper, ProtobufMapper, MapperFeature.BLOCK_UNSAFE_POLYMORPHIC_BASE_TYPES, camel-jackson, camel-jacksonxml, Object, Serializable, Comparable, objectMapper | The `camel-jackson-avro` and `camel-jackson-protobuf` data formats now create their default `AvroMapper` / `ProtobufMapper` with `MapperFeature.BLOCK_UNSAFE_POLYMORPHIC_BASE_TYPES` enabled, mirroring the same hardening applied to `camel-jackson` and `camel-jacksonxml`. This is defense-in-depth against gadget-chain deserialization: when polymorphic / default typing is enabled, Jackson refuses unsafe base types (such as `Object`, `Serializable` or `Comparable`). This only affects routes that enabl | あり | The `camel-jackson-avro` and `camel-jackson-protobuf` data formats now create their default `AvroMapper` /<br>`ProtobufMapper` with `MapperFeature.BLOCK_UNSAFE_POLYMORPHIC_BASE_TYPES` enabled, mirroring the same hardening<br>applied to `camel-jackson` and `camel-jacksonxml`. This is defense-in-depth against gadget-chain deserialization:<br>when polymorphic / default typing is enabled, Jackson refuses unsafe base types (such as `Object`, `Serializable`<br>or `Comparable`).<br><br>This only affects routes that enable polymorphic / default typing on an unsafe base type; ordinary<br>marshalling and unmarshalling are unchanged. If you rely on that behaviour, supply your own mapper<br>(via the `objectMapper` option) configured without this feature. | 未調査 |  |
| C061 | 4.18.1→4.18.3 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-oauth | camel-oauth | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-oauth, UserProfile, JwtTokenValidator | `UserProfile` token verification now fails closed when no JWK set is available: a signed token can no longer be accepted when the configured JWK set is missing or empty, since its signature cannot be verified in that case. Deployments with a correctly resolved JWK set are unaffected; this aligns the legacy `UserProfile` path with the `JwtTokenValidator` SPI path. | あり | `UserProfile` token verification now fails closed when no JWK set is available: a signed token can no<br>longer be accepted when the configured JWK set is missing or empty, since its signature cannot be<br>verified in that case. Deployments with a correctly resolved JWK set are unaffected; this aligns the<br>legacy `UserProfile` path with the `JwtTokenValidator` SPI path. | 未調査 |  |
| C062 | 4.18.1→4.18.3 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-ftp, camel-sftp, camel-mina-sftp, camel-azure-files, camel-smb | camel-ftp, camel-sftp, camel-mina-sftp, camel-azure-files, camel-smb | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-ftp, camel-sftp, camel-mina-sftp, camel-azure-files, camel-smb, localWorkDirectory, ../, jailStartingDirectory, true, jailStartingDirectory=false, GenericFileOperationFailedException | When `localWorkDirectory` is used, the remote-file consumers now ensure the downloaded local work file stays within the configured work directory, so a remote file name containing `../` sequences can no longer resolve to a path outside it. The containment check honours the existing `jailStartingDirectory` option (default `true`); set `jailStartingDirectory=false` to disable it. A remote file that resolves outside the local work directory is rejected with a `GenericFileOperationFailedException`. | あり | When `localWorkDirectory` is used, the remote-file consumers now ensure the downloaded local work file<br>stays within the configured work directory, so a remote file name containing `../` sequences can no longer<br>resolve to a path outside it. The containment check honours the existing `jailStartingDirectory` option<br>(default `true`); set `jailStartingDirectory=false` to disable it. A remote file that resolves outside the<br>local work directory is rejected with a `GenericFileOperationFailedException`. | 未調査 |  |
| C063 | 4.18.1→4.18.3 | パッチ | 高 | 破壊的変更(要確認) | camel-spring-ws | camel-spring-ws - potential breaking change | 原文全文を読み、該当するオプション/クラス/ヘッダー/URI を grep。使用していれば修正が必要 | camel-spring-ws, spring-ws, HeaderFilterStrategy, Exchange, headerFilterStrategy, SpringWebserviceHeaderFilterStrategy, Camel, camel, camel-cxf, camel-mail, camel-coap | The `spring-ws` consumer now applies a `HeaderFilterStrategy` to the SOAP headers it maps onto the Camel `Exchange`. The default `headerFilterStrategy` is a new `SpringWebserviceHeaderFilterStrategy` that filters header names starting with `Camel` / `camel` (case-insensitive) in both the inbound and outbound directions, aligning the component with the rest of the Camel component catalog (`camel-cxf`, `camel-mail`, `camel-coap`, ...). SOAP header element and attribute names that fall in that name | あり | The `spring-ws` consumer now applies a `HeaderFilterStrategy` to the SOAP headers it maps onto the<br>Camel `Exchange`. The default `headerFilterStrategy` is a new `SpringWebserviceHeaderFilterStrategy`<br>that filters header names starting with `Camel` / `camel` (case-insensitive) in both the inbound and<br>outbound directions, aligning the component with the rest of the Camel component catalog<br>(`camel-cxf`, `camel-mail`, `camel-coap`, ...). SOAP header element and attribute names that fall in<br>that namespace are no longer propagated as `Exchange` headers. Routes that relied on receiving such<br>header names from inbound SOAP headers can supply a custom `headerFilterStrategy` (via the new<br>`headerFilterStrategy` endpoint option) to restore the previous behaviour. | 未調査 |  |
| C064 | 4.18.1→4.18.3 | パッチ | 高 | 破壊的変更(要確認) | camel-netty-http, camel-undertow | camel-netty-http / camel-undertow - potential breaking change | 原文全文を読み、該当するオプション/クラス/ヘッダー/URI を grep。使用していれば修正が必要 | camel-netty-http, camel-undertow, muteException, true, camel-netty-http, camel-undertow, camel-http, camel-jetty, camel-servlet, camel-platform-http, text/plain, muteException=false, transferException, transferException=true | The `muteException` consumer option now defaults to `true` in `camel-netty-http` and `camel-undertow`, aligning these components with the other HTTP server components (`camel-http`, `camel-jetty`, `camel-servlet`, and `camel-platform-http`), which have been defaulting `muteException` to `true` for a long time. When an exchange fails processing on the consumer side, the HTTP response now has an empty body. Previously the response body contained the exception stack trace as `text/plain`. Routes th | あり | The `muteException` consumer option now defaults to `true` in `camel-netty-http` and<br>`camel-undertow`, aligning these components with the other HTTP server components<br>(`camel-http`, `camel-jetty`, `camel-servlet`, and `camel-platform-http`), which have<br>been defaulting `muteException` to `true` for a long time.<br><br>When an exchange fails processing on the consumer side, the HTTP response now has an<br>empty body. Previously the response body contained the exception stack trace as<br>`text/plain`.<br><br>Routes that rely on the exception stack trace being present in the response body must<br>set `muteException=false` explicitly on the endpoint or component after the upgrade:<br><br>[source,text]<br>[code]<br>    netty-http:http://0.0.0.0:8080/foo?muteException=false<br>    undertow:http://0.0.0.0:8080/foo?muteException=false<br><br>Note that `muteException` takes precedence over `transferException`, as it already does<br>in the other HTTP server components. Routes using `transferException=true` on these two<br>components must now also set `muteException=false` for the serialized exception to be<br>returned in the response. | 未調査 |  |
| C065 | 4.18.1→4.18.3 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-keycloak | camel-keycloak | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-keycloak, KeycloakSecurityPolicy, requiredRoles, requiredPermissions, CamelAuthorizationException | The `KeycloakSecurityPolicy` route policy now always verifies the access token when one is present - signature, issuer and expiry for local JWT verification, or active state and issuer when token introspection is enabled - even when neither `requiredRoles` nor `requiredPermissions` is configured. Previously the token was only verified when at least one role or permission was required. Routes that attach a `KeycloakSecurityPolicy` without any roles or permissions and that previously forwarded an | あり | The `KeycloakSecurityPolicy` route policy now always verifies the access token when one is present - signature,<br>issuer and expiry for local JWT verification, or active state and issuer when token introspection is enabled -<br>even when neither `requiredRoles` nor `requiredPermissions` is configured. Previously the token was only verified<br>when at least one role or permission was required.<br><br>Routes that attach a `KeycloakSecurityPolicy` without any roles or permissions and that previously forwarded an<br>unverified or invalid token will now have such requests rejected with a `CamelAuthorizationException`. Provide a<br>valid, verifiable token (or configure `requiredRoles` / `requiredPermissions`) for these routes. | 未調査 |  |
| C066 | 4.18.1→4.18.3 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-whatsapp | camel-whatsapp | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-whatsapp, camel-whatsapp, webhookSecret, X-Hub-Signature-256 | The `camel-whatsapp` webhook consumer now supports optional verification of inbound webhook event callbacks via the new `webhookSecret` endpoint option. When set, event callbacks whose `X-Hub-Signature-256` HMAC-SHA256 signature is missing or invalid are rejected with HTTP 403; when the option is not set, behaviour is unchanged. | あり | The `camel-whatsapp` webhook consumer now supports optional verification of inbound webhook event<br>callbacks via the new `webhookSecret` endpoint option. When set, event callbacks whose<br>`X-Hub-Signature-256` HMAC-SHA256 signature is missing or invalid are rejected with HTTP 403; when<br>the option is not set, behaviour is unchanged. | 未調査 |  |
