| C151 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 高 | 削除 | camel-cloud | camel-cloud (Removal) | pom/gradle の依存、URIスキーム(例: xxx:)、import、DSL要素を grep。代替先が記載されていれば置換計画を立てる | camel-cloud, camel-cloud, serviceCall, camel-service, camel-consul, camel-dns, camel-http, camel-jetty, camel-kubernetes, camel-netty-http, camel-zookeeper | The `camel-cloud` module and the `serviceCall` EIP have been removed. These were deprecated in Camel 3.19 and 4.7. The `camel-service` component has also been removed. The cloud integration from the following components has been removed: `camel-consul`, `camel-dns`, `camel-http`, `camel-jetty`, `camel-kubernetes`, `camel-netty-http`, and `camel-zookeeper`. |  | The `camel-cloud` module and the `serviceCall` EIP have been removed. These were deprecated in Camel 3.19 and 4.7.<br>The `camel-service` component has also been removed.<br><br>The cloud integration from the following components has been removed: `camel-consul`, `camel-dns`, `camel-http`, `camel-jetty`, `camel-kubernetes`, `camel-netty-http`, and `camel-zookeeper`. | 未調査 |  |
| C152 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-core | camel-core | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-core, X25519MLKEM768, SSLContextParameters, x25519, secp256r1, secp384r1, namedGroups, namedGroupsFilter, pattern, InOnly, throttler, ErrorRegistry, CamelContext, <compensation> | When running on a JDK that supports `X25519MLKEM768` (typically JDK 25+), Camel now automatically configures post-quantum hybrid named groups on all `SSLContextParameters` instances. The preferred group ordering is: `X25519MLKEM768`, `x25519`, `secp256r1`, `secp384r1`, followed by the remaining JVM defaults. This auto-configuration activates only when the user has not explicitly set `namedGroups` or `namedGroupsFilter`. No changes are required for existing applications — the hybrid key exchange | あり | ## PQC TLS Auto-Configuration<br><br>When running on a JDK that supports `X25519MLKEM768` (typically JDK 25+), Camel now automatically<br>configures post-quantum hybrid named groups on all `SSLContextParameters` instances. The preferred<br>group ordering is: `X25519MLKEM768`, `x25519`, `secp256r1`, `secp384r1`, followed by the remaining<br>JVM defaults.<br><br>This auto-configuration activates only when the user has not explicitly set `namedGroups` or<br>`namedGroupsFilter`. No changes are required for existing applications — the hybrid key exchange<br>is backward-compatible with peers that do not support PQC.<br><br>See xref:camel-configuration-utilities.adoc[JSSE Utility] for full details on PQC TLS configuration.<br><br>The WireTap EIP has removed the `pattern` option from its model (not in use) as wiretap always<br>uses `InOnly` pattern.<br><br>Removed 2 deprecated methods in Java DSL for `throttler` EIP.<br><br>## ErrorRegistry<br><br>A new `ErrorRegistry` SPI has been added to `CamelContext` for capturing routing errors.<br>See xref:error-registry.adoc[Error Registry] for more details.<br><br>## Saga EIP<br><br>The Saga EIP has _fixed_ the model for how to configure completion and compensation URIs.<br><br>For Java DSL there is no changes, but XML and YAML DSL is affected. Here the `<compensation>` and `<completion>` tags<br>has been changed to be an attribute on `<saga>` instead as shown below:<br><br>Before:<br><br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <route><br>        <from uri="direct:start"/><br>        <saga sagaService="mySagaService"><br>            <compensation uri="mock:compensation"/><br>            <completion uri="mock:completion"/><br>            <option key="myOptionKey"><br>                <constant>myOptionValue</constant><br>            </option><br>            <option key="myOptionKey2"><br>                <constant>myOptionValue2</constant><br>            </option><br>        </saga><br>        <choice><br>            <when><br>                <simple>${body} == 'fail'</simple><br>                <throwException exceptionType="java.lang.RuntimeException" message="fail"/><br>            </when><br>        </choice><br>        <to uri="mock:end"/><br>    </route><br><br>In YAML DSL the changes are even simpler as the endpoint is moved from `uri` to the value of `completion` or `compensation`.<br><br>[source,yaml]<br>[code]<br>    - route:<br>        from:<br>          uri: direct:start<br>          steps:<br>            - saga:<br>                sagaService: mySagaService<br>                compensation:<br>                  uri: mock:compensation<br>                completion:<br>                  uri: mock:completion<br>                option:<br>                  - key: myOptionKey<br>                    expression:<br>                      constant:<br>                        expression: myOptionValue<br>                  - key: myOptionKey2<br>                    expression:<br>                      constant:<br>                        expression: myOptionValue2<br>            - choice:<br>                when:<br>                  - expression:<br>                      simple:<br>                        expression: "${body} == 'fail'"<br>                    steps:<br>                      - throwException:<br>                          message: fail<br>                          exceptionType: java.lang.RuntimeException<br>            - to:<br>                uri: mock:end<br>    <br><br>After:<br><br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <route><br>        <from uri="direct:start"/><br>        <saga sagaService="mySagaService" compensation="mock:compensation" completion="mock:completion"><br>            <option key="myOptionKey"><br>                <constant>myOptionValue</constant><br>            </option><br>            <option key="myOptionKey2"><br>                <constant>myOptionValue2</constant><br>            </option><br>        </saga><br>        <choice><br>            <when><br>                <simple>${body} == 'fail'</simple><br>                <throwException exceptionType="java.lang.RuntimeException" message="fail"/><br>            </when><br>        </choice><br>        <to uri="mock:end"/><br>    </route><br><br>[source,yaml]<br>[code]<br>    - route:<br>        from:<br>          uri: direct:start<br>          steps:<br>            - saga:<br>                sagaService: mySagaService<br>                compensation: mock:compensation<br>                completion: mock:completion<br>                option:<br>                  - key: myOptionKey<br>                    expression:<br>                      constant:<br>                        expression: myOptionValue<br>                  - key: myOptionKey2<br>                    expression:<br>                      constant:<br>                        expression: myOptionValue2<br>            - choice:<br>                when:<br>                  - expression:<br>                      simple:<br>                        expression: "${body} == 'fail'"<br>                    steps:<br>                      - throwException:<br>                          message: fail<br>                          exceptionType: java.lang.RuntimeException<br>            - to:<br>                uri: mock:end | 未調査 |  |
| C153 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-platform-http-main | camel-platform-http-main | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-platform-http-main, authenticationEnabled, true, authenticationPath, /*, path, /api | When `authenticationEnabled` is set to `true` and no explicit `authenticationPath` is configured, the default authentication path is now `/*`. This means all subpaths under the configured context path are protected by authentication. Previously, the authentication path defaulted to the value of `path` (e.g. `/api`), which only covered that exact path. If you relied on this behavior and need selective path protection, set `authenticationPath` explicitly: | あり | When `authenticationEnabled` is set to `true` and no explicit `authenticationPath` is configured,<br>the default authentication path is now `/*`. This means all subpaths under the configured context path<br>are protected by authentication.<br><br>Previously, the authentication path defaulted to the value of `path` (e.g. `/api`), which only covered<br>that exact path. If you relied on this behavior and need selective path protection, set<br>`authenticationPath` explicitly:<br><br>[source,properties]<br>[code]<br>    camel.server.authenticationPath=/secure/* | 未調査 |  |
| C154 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 中 | 非推奨 | camel-csimple | camel-csimple (Deprecation) | 使用有無を grep。今回の更新では動く想定だが、次回以降の削除に備えて代替先を確認 | camel-csimple, csimple, simple, camel-csimple-joor | The `csimple` (compiled simple) language has been deprecated. Use the `simple` language instead. The `camel-csimple-joor` module is also deprecated. The csimple language and related modules will be removed in a future release. |  | The `csimple` (compiled simple) language has been deprecated. Use the `simple` language instead.<br>The `camel-csimple-joor` module is also deprecated. The csimple language and related modules<br>will be removed in a future release. | 未調査 |  |
| C155 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 高 | オプション/クラス/API名・形式の変更 | camel-simple | camel-simple | 旧名称(オプション名・クラス名・ヘッダー名・XML/YAML属性)を grep し、新名称へ置換。XML/YAML DSL は属性形式の変更もあるため route ファイルも対象 | camel-simple | In the simple language then init blocks syntax has changed to require that each variable ends with a semicolon and new line (no trailing comments etc is allowed) For example Should be changed to have semicolons as shown below: | あり | In the simple language then init blocks syntax has changed to require that each variable ends with a semicolon and new line (no trailing comments etc is allowed)<br><br>For example<br><br>[source,yaml]<br>[code]<br>        - setBody:<br>            simple:<br>              expression: \|-<br>                $init{<br>                  // this is a java like comment<br>                  $sum := ${sum(${header.lines},100)}<br>    <br>                  $sku := ${iif(${body} contains 'Camel',123,999)}<br>                }init$<br>                orderId=$sku,total=$sum<br><br>Should be changed to have semicolons as shown below:<br><br>[source,yaml]<br>[code]<br>        - setBody:<br>            simple:<br>              expression: \|-<br>                $init{<br>                  // this is a java like comment<br>                  $sum := ${sum(${header.lines},100)};<br>    <br>                  $sku := ${iif(${body} contains 'Camel',123,999)};<br>                }init$<br>                orderId=$sku,total=$sum | 未調査 |  |
| C156 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-test-infra | camel-test-infra | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-test-infra, test-jar, camel-test-infra-*, <type>test-jar</type>, <type>, camel-test-infra-common | The test infrastructure modules no longer produce `test-jar` artifacts. All classes (service interfaces, container implementations, JUnit extensions, and service factories) are now packaged in the regular JAR artifact. If your project depends on `camel-test-infra-*` modules with `<type>test-jar</type>`, remove the `<type>` element: Before: After: This applies to all `camel-test-infra-*` artifacts, including `camel-test-infra-common`. |  | The test infrastructure modules no longer produce `test-jar` artifacts. All classes (service interfaces,<br>container implementations, JUnit extensions, and service factories) are now packaged in the regular JAR artifact.<br><br>If your project depends on `camel-test-infra-*` modules with `<type>test-jar</type>`, remove the `<type>` element:<br><br>Before:<br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <dependency><br>        <groupId>org.apache.camel</groupId><br>        <artifactId>camel-test-infra-kafka</artifactId><br>        <version>${camel.version}</version><br>        <type>test-jar</type><br>        <scope>test</scope><br>    </dependency><br><br>After:<br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <dependency><br>        <groupId>org.apache.camel</groupId><br>        <artifactId>camel-test-infra-kafka</artifactId><br>        <version>${camel.version}</version><br>        <scope>test</scope><br>    </dependency><br><br>This applies to all `camel-test-infra-*` artifacts, including `camel-test-infra-common`. | 未調査 |  |
| C157 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 高 | オプション/クラス/API名・形式の変更 | camel-yaml-io, camel-xml-io | camel-yaml-io / camel-xml-io | 旧名称(オプション名・クラス名・ヘッダー名・XML/YAML属性)を grep し、新名称へ置換。XML/YAML DSL は属性形式の変更もあるため route ファイルも対象 | camel-yaml-io, camel-xml-io, routePolicy, routePolicyRef, route, camel-yaml-io, camel-xml-io, id, circuitBreaker, onFallback | In the YAML DSL we have renamed `routePolicy` to `routePolicyRef` on the `route` node, as that is the correct name. When dumping routes in YAML or XML format via `camel-yaml-io` or `camel-xml-io` then the structure of routes and all the EIP options now respect the intended order in the model. For example `id` is always first, and the following attributes are ordered so the most commonly used at in the top. EIPs such as `circuitBreaker` now has `onFallback` last. This order is also the same order | あり | In the YAML DSL we have renamed `routePolicy` to `routePolicyRef` on the `route` node,<br>as that is the correct name.<br><br>When dumping routes in YAML or XML format via `camel-yaml-io` or `camel-xml-io` then the structure of routes<br>and all the EIP options now respect the intended order in the model.<br><br>For example `id` is always first, and the following attributes are ordered so the most<br>commonly used at in the top. EIPs such as `circuitBreaker` now has `onFallback` last.<br><br>This order is also the same order that UI builders like Camel Karavan and Kaoto do as well. | 未調査 |  |
| C158 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 低 | 追加/機能拡張・ライブラリ更新(参考) | (全般/その他) | Jackson 3 components | 参考情報。ただしライブラリのメジャー更新を含む場合は原文で破壊的変更の有無を確認 |  | Four new components have been added which provide Jackson 3 support - they are named similarly to the previously existing camel-jackson components. Jackson 3 operates under a different package name (tools.jackson.* vs. com.fasterxml.jackson) and there are a number of API changes between Jackson 2 and Jackson 3 - see the Jackson Migration Guide for details. .Jackson Components \|Jackson 2 component \|Jackson 3 component \|camel-jackson \|camel-jackson3 \|camel-jackson-avro \|camel-jackson3-avro \|camel- |  | Four new components have been added which provide Jackson 3 support - they are named similarly to the previously existing camel-jackson components.   Jackson 3 operates under a different package name (tools.jackson.* vs. com.fasterxml.jackson) and there are a number of API changes between Jackson 2 and Jackson 3 - see the  https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson/blob/main/jackson3/MIGRATING_TO_JACKSON_3.md[Jackson Migration Guide] for details.<br><br>  .Jackson Components<br>  [cols="1,1",options="header"]<br>  \|===<br>  \|Jackson 2 component \|Jackson 3 component<br><br>  \|camel-jackson<br>  \|camel-jackson3<br><br>  \|camel-jackson-avro<br>  \|camel-jackson3-avro<br><br>  \|camel-jackson-protobuf<br>  \|camel-jackson3-protobuf<br><br>  \|camel-jacksonxml<br>  \|camel-jackson3xml<br>  \|===<br><br>The camel-jackson3 component shares a unified DSL with the camel-jackson component under the "jackson" name.   DefaultDataFormatResolver and DefaultTransformerResolver resolve which Jackson library version is available on the classpath and choose the appropriate data format or transformer.   This allows easy migration from the camel-jackson component to the camel-jackson3 component and a consistent interface between the two.<br><br>The same detection mechanism and combined interface extends to the other Jackson data formats (avroJackson, protobufJackson, and jacksonXml). | 未調査 |  |
| C159 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 高 | オプション/クラス/API名・形式の変更 | camel-test-junit6, camel-test-main-junit6, camel-test-spring-junit6 | camel-test-junit6, camel-test-main-junit6, camel-test-spring-junit6 | 旧名称(オプション名・クラス名・ヘッダー名・XML/YAML属性)を grep し、新名称へ置換。XML/YAML DSL は属性形式の変更もあるため route ファイルも対象 | camel-test-junit6, camel-test-main-junit6, camel-test-spring-junit6 | camel-test-junit6 was introduced in 4.17.0 - and in 4.19.0 all of the camel components have moved to using it for testing as part of the upgrade to Spring Boot 4.0. Migration to JUnit 6 camel-test-* components is optional - the camel-test-junit5 is still available and is pinned to JUnit 5 use. Migrating to camel-test-junit6 has the benefit of better alignment with Spring Boot 4.0 (using camel-spring-boot as a runtime). If you are using camel-test-junit5 and would like to move to camel-test-junit |  | camel-test-junit6 was introduced in 4.17.0 - and in 4.19.0 all of the camel components have moved to using it for testing as part of the upgrade to Spring Boot 4.0.   Migration to JUnit 6 camel-test-* components is optional - the camel-test-junit5 is still available and is pinned to JUnit 5 use.   Migrating to camel-test-junit6 has the benefit of better alignment with Spring Boot 4.0 (using camel-spring-boot as a runtime).  If you are using camel-test-junit5 and would like to move to camel-test-junit6, you can change from:<br><br>Before:<br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <dependency><br>        <groupId>org.apache.camel</groupId><br>        <artifactId>camel-test-junit5</artifactId><br>        <version>${camel.version}</version><br>        <scope>test</scope><br>    </dependency><br><br>After:<br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <dependency><br>        <groupId>org.apache.camel</groupId><br>        <artifactId>camel-test-junit6</artifactId><br>        <version>${camel.version}</version><br>        <scope>test</scope><br>    </dependency><br><br>You will also need to change any imports of classes in `+org.apache.camel.test.junit5.*+` to `+import org.apache.camel.test.junit6.*+`.<br><br>Similarly, for camel-test-main-junit5 you would need to change any imports of classes in `+org.apache.camel.test.main.junit5.*+` to `+org.apache.camel.test.main.junit6.*+`, and the dependency in your pom.xml would change from:<br><br>Before:<br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <dependency><br>        <groupId>org.apache.camel</groupId><br>        <artifactId>camel-test-main-junit5</artifactId><br>        <version>${camel.version}</version><br>        <scope>test</scope><br>    </dependency><br><br>After:<br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <dependency><br>        <groupId>org.apache.camel</groupId><br>        <artifactId>camel-test-main-junit6</artifactId><br>        <version>${camel.version}</version><br>        <scope>test</scope><br>    </dependency><br><br>Finally, for camel-test-spring-junit5 any imports would change from `+org.apache.camel.test.spring.junit5.*+` to `+import org.apache.camel.test.spring.junit6.*+` and the dependency change would be :<br><br>Before:<br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <dependency><br>        <groupId>org.apache.camel</groupId><br>        <artifactId>camel-test-spring-junit5</artifactId><br>        <version>${camel.version}</version><br>        <scope>test</scope><br>    </dependency><br><br>After:<br>[source,xml]<br>[code]<br>    <dependency><br>        <groupId>org.apache.camel</groupId><br>        <artifactId>camel-test-spring-junit6</artifactId><br>        <version>${camel.version}</version><br>        <scope>test</scope><br>    </dependency> | 未調査 |  |
| C160 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 高 | 削除 | camel-jbang | camel-jbang | pom/gradle の依存、URIスキーム(例: xxx:)、import、DSL要素を grep。代替先が記載されていれば置換計画を立てる | camel-jbang, buildToool, gradleWrapper, camel-tooling-maven | Support for exporting to use Gradle as build tool has been removed (it was deprecated and not working well) The deprecated options `buildToool` and `gradleWrapper` has been removed. The `camel-tooling-maven` which is used for downloading JARs from Maven has been refactored to use the new MIMA project (jbang is using this also). | あり | Support for exporting to use Gradle as build tool has been removed (it was deprecated and not working well)<br>The deprecated options `buildToool` and `gradleWrapper` has been removed.<br><br>The `camel-tooling-maven` which is used for downloading JARs from Maven has been refactored to use<br>the new https://github.com/maveniverse/mima[MIMA] project (jbang is using this also). | 未調査 |  |
| C161 | 4.18→4.19 | マイナー | 低 | 追加/機能拡張・ライブラリ更新(参考) | camel-groovy | camel-groovy | 参考情報。ただしライブラリのメジャー更新を含む場合は原文で破壊的変更の有無を確認 | camel-groovy | The Groovy library has been upgraded from 4.0.x to 5.0.x. This is a major version upgrade. If you use Groovy scripts or the Groovy DSL, review the Groovy 5.0 release notes for potential breaking changes. The Spock testing framework has also been upgraded to 2.4-groovy-5.0. |  | The Groovy library has been upgraded from 4.0.x to 5.0.x. This is a major version upgrade.<br>If you use Groovy scripts or the Groovy DSL, review the<br>https://groovy-lang.org/releasenotes/groovy-5.0.html[Groovy 5.0 release notes] for potential breaking changes.<br>The Spock testing framework has also been upgraded to 2.4-groovy-5.0. | 未調査 |  |
