| C211 | 4.20→4.21 | マイナー | 低 | 追加/機能拡張・ライブラリ更新(参考) | camel-elasticsearch, camel-elasticsearch-rest-client, camel-solr | camel-elasticsearch / camel-elasticsearch-rest-client / camel-solr | 参考情報。ただしライブラリのメジャー更新を含む場合は原文で破壊的変更の有無を確認 | camel-elasticsearch, camel-elasticsearch-rest-client, camel-solr, camel-elasticsearch, camel-elasticsearch-rest-client, camel-solr, SSLContextParameters, certificatePath, sslContextParameters, X25519MLKEM768, useGlobalSslContextParameters, user, password | The `camel-elasticsearch`, `camel-elasticsearch-rest-client` and `camel-solr` components now support configuring TLS through `SSLContextParameters` (the JSSE utility), in addition to the existing `certificatePath` option. The new `sslContextParameters` option allows configuring named groups, signature schemes, cipher suites and protocols, for example post-quantum named groups such as `X25519MLKEM768` on JDK 25+. It can be set at the endpoint or component level, and the components also honor the |  | The `camel-elasticsearch`, `camel-elasticsearch-rest-client` and `camel-solr` components now support<br>configuring TLS through `SSLContextParameters` (the JSSE utility), in addition to the existing<br>`certificatePath` option. The new `sslContextParameters` option allows configuring named groups,<br>signature schemes, cipher suites and protocols, for example post-quantum named groups such as<br>`X25519MLKEM768` on JDK 25+. It can be set at the endpoint or component level, and the components also<br>honor the context-wide global SSL configuration via `useGlobalSslContextParameters`. When configured,<br>`SSLContextParameters` takes precedence over `certificatePath`.<br><br>For `camel-elasticsearch` and `camel-elasticsearch-rest-client`, the HTTP client is now configured with<br>the TLS settings regardless of whether basic authentication (`user`/`password`) is set. Previously the<br>`certificatePath` option was silently ignored unless both `user` and `password` were configured. Routes<br>that set `certificatePath` without credentials will now correctly use the configured TLS context where it<br>was previously a no-op. | 未調査 |  |
| C212 | 4.20→4.21 | マイナー | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-openai | camel-openai | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-openai, chat-completion, WrappedFile, Path, byte[], InputStream, java.io.File, CamelOpenAIMediaType, CamelFileContentType, CamelAwsS3ContentType, Content-Type, Files.probeContentType(), application/xml, application/json | The `chat-completion` operation now accepts `WrappedFile` (the body type produced by the file, FTP, SFTP and SMB components), `Path`, `byte[]` and `InputStream` message bodies for file-based and vision model input, in addition to `java.io.File`. Previously such bodies were converted to a String, which corrupted binary image content. The MIME type of the body is now detected from headers (the new `CamelOpenAIMediaType` header, `CamelFileContentType`, cloud storage content-type headers such as `Ca | あり | The `chat-completion` operation now accepts `WrappedFile` (the body type produced by the file, FTP, SFTP and SMB<br>components), `Path`, `byte[]` and `InputStream` message bodies for file-based and vision model input, in addition<br>to `java.io.File`. Previously such bodies were converted to a String, which corrupted binary image content.<br><br>The MIME type of the body is now detected from headers (the new `CamelOpenAIMediaType` header, `CamelFileContentType`,<br>cloud storage content-type headers such as `CamelAwsS3ContentType`, or `Content-Type`), and finally the file name<br>extension using the Camel built-in MIME type table. Previously only `Files.probeContentType()` was used, which could<br>fail to detect the type on some platforms. A `byte[]` or `InputStream` body whose detected MIME type is an image is now<br>sent to the model as a base64-encoded image instead of being converted to text; bodies without image MIME type metadata<br>keep the previous text behavior. XML and JSON files (`application/xml`, `application/json`) are treated as text prompts.<br><br>The `sse` `transportType` is deprecated. it is recommended to switch to `streamableHttp`. | 未調査 |  |
