| C270 | 4.20→4.21 | マイナー | 中 | 非推奨 | camel-jasypt | Deprecation of camel-jasypt CLI entrypoint | 使用有無を grep。今回の更新では動く想定だが、次回以降の削除に備えて代替先を確認 | camel-jasypt, org.apache.camel.component.jasypt.Main, camel-jasypt, encrypt.sh, decrypt.sh, digest.sh | The `org.apache.camel.component.jasypt.Main` class — the command line entrypoint that lets the `camel-jasypt` jar be invoked directly (e.g. via JBang) to encrypt or decrypt property values — is now deprecated and will be removed in a future Camel release. Use the standalone CLI scripts (`encrypt.sh` / `decrypt.sh` / `digest.sh`) shipped in the upstream link:jasypt-1.9.3 distribution instead. They cover the same workflow and let us drop the duplicate implementation maintained inside `camel-jasypt |  | The `org.apache.camel.component.jasypt.Main` class — the command line entrypoint that lets the `camel-jasypt`<br>jar be invoked directly (e.g. via JBang) to encrypt or decrypt property values — is now deprecated and will be<br>removed in a future Camel release.<br><br>Use the standalone CLI scripts (`encrypt.sh` / `decrypt.sh` / `digest.sh`) shipped in the upstream<br>link:https://github.com/jasypt/jasypt/releases/tag/jasypt-1.9.3[jasypt-1.9.3 distribution] instead. They cover<br>the same workflow and let us drop the duplicate implementation maintained inside `camel-jasypt`. The component<br>itself (property-source decryption at runtime) is unaffected. | 未調査 |  |
| C271 | 4.20→4.21 | マイナー | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-langchain4j-tools, camel-langchain4j-agent, camel-spring-ai-tools | camel-langchain4j-tools / camel-langchain4j-agent / camel-spring-ai-tools | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-langchain4j-tools, camel-langchain4j-agent, camel-spring-ai-tools, parameter.<name>, parameter.*, camel-langchain4j-agent, int, long, double, boolean, String, JsonNode | Tool argument headers are now filtered against the tool's declared parameter schema. When the LLM returns a tool call, only JSON field names that match a declared `parameter.<name>` are set as Exchange headers. Undeclared field names are logged at WARN level and skipped. This is a breaking change for tools defined without explicit `parameter.*` declarations. Previously, all LLM-provided argument field names were set as Exchange headers without filtering. Now, tools with no declared parameters wi |  | Tool argument headers are now filtered against the tool's declared parameter schema. When the LLM returns<br>a tool call, only JSON field names that match a declared `parameter.<name>` are set as Exchange headers.<br>Undeclared field names are logged at WARN level and skipped.<br><br>This is a breaking change for tools defined without explicit `parameter.*` declarations. Previously, all<br>LLM-provided argument field names were set as Exchange headers without filtering. Now, tools with no<br>declared parameters will have zero argument headers set from the LLM tool call.<br><br>For example, a tool defined as:<br><br>._Java-only: tool route without declared parameters_<br>[source,java]<br>[code]<br>    from("langchain4j-tools:test1?tags=user&description=Does not really do anything")<br><br>will no longer receive any LLM-provided arguments as headers. To restore argument flow, declare the<br>expected parameters explicitly:<br><br>._Java-only: tool route with declared parameters_<br>[source,java]<br>[code]<br>    from("langchain4j-tools:test1?tags=user&description=Query user by number&parameter.number=integer")<br><br>Additionally, `camel-langchain4j-agent` now extracts primitive values (`int`, `long`, `double`, `boolean`,<br>`String`) from tool arguments instead of setting raw `JsonNode` objects as headers. | 未調査 |  |
| C272 | 4.20→4.21 | マイナー | 中 | 非推奨 | camel-headersmap | Deprecation of camel-headersmap | 使用有無を grep。今回の更新では動く想定だが、次回以降の削除に備えて代替先を確認 | camel-headersmap, CaseInsensitiveMap, java-util, camel-headersmap | The component camel-headersmap is deprecated. Since Camel 4.21, the default `CaseInsensitiveMap` in camel-core uses a custom O(1) hash table with zero-allocation lookups and header key deduplication, making the external cedarsoftware `java-util` dependency unnecessary. Simply remove the `camel-headersmap` dependency from your project — the core implementation now provides equivalent or better performance. |  | The component camel-headersmap is deprecated. Since Camel 4.21, the default `CaseInsensitiveMap` in camel-core<br>uses a custom O(1) hash table with zero-allocation lookups and header key deduplication, making the external<br>cedarsoftware `java-util` dependency unnecessary. Simply remove the `camel-headersmap` dependency from your<br>project — the core implementation now provides equivalent or better performance. | 未調査 |  |
