| C315 | 4.21→4.22 | マイナー | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-kafka | camel-kafka - saslAuthType behavior changes | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-kafka, saslAuthType, putIfAbsent, saslJaasConfig, saslAuthType=OAUTH, clientId, clientSecret, scope, oauth.token.endpoint.uri, saslAuthType=KERBEROS, java.security.auth.login.config | When `saslAuthType` is set, the generated JAAS configuration and additional SASL properties are now applied using `putIfAbsent` semantics, so explicitly configured `saslJaasConfig`, callback handler classes, or token endpoint URLs take precedence over the auto-generated values. For OAuth (`saslAuthType=OAUTH`), the JAAS string now contains only login-module parameters (`clientId`, `clientSecret`, `scope`). The `oauth.token.endpoint.uri` and callback handler class are set as separate Kafka client |  | When `saslAuthType` is set, the generated JAAS configuration and additional SASL properties are now<br>applied using `putIfAbsent` semantics, so explicitly configured `saslJaasConfig`, callback handler<br>classes, or token endpoint URLs take precedence over the auto-generated values.<br><br>For OAuth (`saslAuthType=OAUTH`), the JAAS string now contains only login-module parameters<br>(`clientId`, `clientSecret`, `scope`). The `oauth.token.endpoint.uri` and callback handler<br>class are set as separate Kafka client properties instead of being embedded in the JAAS string,<br>matching the Kafka client's expected configuration format.<br><br>For Kerberos (`saslAuthType=KERBEROS`), if the principal is not configured, the configurer now<br>assumes an external JAAS configuration (e.g. via `java.security.auth.login.config`) and skips<br>JAAS string generation instead of throwing an exception. This supports deployment scenarios<br>where Kerberos is configured externally. | 未調査 |  |
| C316 | 4.21→4.22 | マイナー | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-kafka | camel-kafka - Producer no longer silently drops scalar Jackson nodes | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-kafka, useIterator=true, Iterable, JsonNode, IntNode, transform().jq(".my-value"), ArrayNode, ObjectNode, convertBodyTo(...) | With `useIterator=true`, the Kafka producer splits an `Iterable` body into one record per element. A Jackson `JsonNode` implements `Iterable`, so a scalar value node (e.g. an `IntNode` produced by `transform().jq(".my-value")`) was seen as an empty iterable and produced no record, silently discarding the message with no exception or log. Scalar value nodes are now sent as a single record. Only container nodes (`ArrayNode`, `ObjectNode`) are still split, which is unchanged. Any `convertBodyTo(... |  | With `useIterator=true`, the Kafka producer splits an `Iterable` body into one record per element.<br>A Jackson `JsonNode` implements `Iterable`, so a scalar value node (e.g. an `IntNode` produced by<br>`transform().jq(".my-value")`) was seen as an empty iterable and produced no record, silently<br>discarding the message with no exception or log.<br><br>Scalar value nodes are now sent as a single record. Only container nodes (`ArrayNode`, `ObjectNode`)<br>are still split, which is unchanged. Any `convertBodyTo(...)` previously used as a workaround is no<br>longer required. | 未調査 |  |
| C317 | 4.21→4.22 | マイナー | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-kafka | camel-kafka - sslEndpointAlgorithm=none now disables hostname verification | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-kafka, sslEndpointAlgorithm, none, false, ssl.endpoint.identification.algorithm | Setting `sslEndpointAlgorithm` to `none` or `false` now correctly disables SSL hostname verification by setting `ssl.endpoint.identification.algorithm` to an empty string. Previously the property was simply omitted, which caused Kafka clients to fall back to their default (`https`), leaving hostname verification silently enabled. |  | Setting `sslEndpointAlgorithm` to `none` or `false` now correctly disables SSL hostname verification<br>by setting `ssl.endpoint.identification.algorithm` to an empty string. Previously the property was<br>simply omitted, which caused Kafka clients to fall back to their default (`https`), leaving hostname<br>verification silently enabled. | 未調査 |  |
| C318 | 4.21→4.22 | マイナー | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-kafka | camel-kafka - Auto-generated groupId shared across consumer threads | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-kafka, groupId, consumersCount | When no `groupId` is configured, the auto-generated UUID is now shared across all consumer threads (`consumersCount`). Previously each thread received its own random UUID, causing each thread to independently consume all partitions, which resulted in every message being processed `consumersCount` times. |  | When no `groupId` is configured, the auto-generated UUID is now shared across all consumer threads<br>(`consumersCount`). Previously each thread received its own random UUID, causing each thread to<br>independently consume all partitions, which resulted in every message being processed `consumersCount`<br>times. | 未調査 |  |
| C319 | 4.21→4.22 | マイナー | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-kafka | camel-kafka - Batch producer respects endpoint key for plain list elements | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-kafka, List, key, CamelKafkaKey, key=fixedKey, Exchange, Message | The batch producer (when the body is a `List`) now respects the endpoint-configured `key` option for elements that do not have a `CamelKafkaKey` header. Previously, elements without the header would get a null record key even when `key=fixedKey` was configured on the endpoint. Additionally, plain list elements (not `Exchange` or `Message`) are now properly converted to the configured serializer type. |  | The batch producer (when the body is a `List`) now respects the endpoint-configured `key` option for<br>elements that do not have a `CamelKafkaKey` header. Previously, elements without the header would<br>get a null record key even when `key=fixedKey` was configured on the endpoint. Additionally, plain<br>list elements (not `Exchange` or `Message`) are now properly converted to the configured serializer<br>type. | 未調査 |  |
