| C386 | 4.22.0→4.22.1 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-spring-redis | camel-spring-redis - the default serializer applies a deserialization filter | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-spring-redis, JdkSerializationRedisSerializer, java.io.ObjectInputFilter, DeserializationFilterHelper, jdk.serialFilter, java.net.**, deserializationFilter, serializer, RedisSerializer | The default serializer, `JdkSerializationRedisSerializer`, now installs a JEP-290 `java.io.ObjectInputFilter` while reading Redis payloads, resolved through `DeserializationFilterHelper`. Previously no filter was applied at all. This affects both the consumer, which deserializes the payload of every message published to the subscribed channels, and the producer read commands, which deserialize the values stored in Redis. When no explicit pattern is configured, the JVM-wide `jdk.serialFilter` is | あり | The default serializer, `JdkSerializationRedisSerializer`, now installs a JEP-290<br>`java.io.ObjectInputFilter` while reading Redis payloads, resolved through<br>`DeserializationFilterHelper`. Previously no filter was applied at all. This affects both the<br>consumer, which deserializes the payload of every message published to the subscribed channels,<br>and the producer read commands, which deserialize the values stored in Redis.<br><br>When no explicit pattern is configured, the JVM-wide `jdk.serialFilter` is honoured if set,<br>otherwise the shared Camel default allow-list is applied (it permits standard Java and Apache Camel<br>types, denies `java.net.**`, and enforces JEP-290 graph-shape limits). Routes that exchange classes<br>outside that allow-list must widen it through the new `deserializationFilter` endpoint option, for<br>example:<br><br>[source,java]<br>[code]<br>    from("spring-redis://localhost:6379?command=SUBSCRIBE&channels=myChannel"<br>         + "&deserializationFilter=com.example.model.**;java.**;!*")<br><br>Setting the `serializer` option to a custom `RedisSerializer` bypasses the filter entirely, since<br>Camel then no longer controls how the payload is read. | 未調査 |  |
| C387 | 4.22.0→4.22.1 | パッチ | 高 | 削除 | camel-infinispan | camel-infinispan - the aggregation repository keeps completed exchanges for recovery | pom/gradle の依存、URIスキーム(例: xxx:)、import、DSL要素を grep。代替先が記載されていれば置換計画を立てる | camel-infinispan, InfinispanAggregationRepository, RecoverableAggregationRepository, remove, confirm, scan, CamelRedelivered, maximumRedeliveries, camel-recovery:<exchange id>, recover, getKeys, useRecovery=false | `InfinispanAggregationRepository` implements `RecoverableAggregationRepository`, but it had no recovery store: `remove` deleted the completed exchange outright, `confirm` removed the exchange id from a cache keyed by correlation key, and `scan` returned the correlation keys of the aggregations still in progress. The recovery task therefore re-delivered aggregations that were still accumulating, marked them `CamelRedelivered`, and sent them to the dead letter channel once `maximumRedeliveries` wa | あり | `InfinispanAggregationRepository` implements `RecoverableAggregationRepository`, but it had no recovery<br>store: `remove` deleted the completed exchange outright, `confirm` removed the exchange id from a cache<br>keyed by correlation key, and `scan` returned the correlation keys of the aggregations still in progress.<br>The recovery task therefore re-delivered aggregations that were still accumulating, marked them<br>`CamelRedelivered`, and sent them to the dead letter channel once `maximumRedeliveries` was reached, while<br>exchanges that genuinely failed after completion could never be recovered.<br><br>A completed exchange is now kept in the same cache under a `camel-recovery:<exchange id>` key until it is<br>confirmed, which is what `scan` reports and `recover` reads. `getKeys` continues to report only the<br>aggregations in progress.<br><br>Routes that set `useRecovery=false` are unaffected. Routes that left recovery enabled, which is the<br>default, stop seeing in-progress aggregations re-delivered, and start seeing genuine recovery. The cache<br>now also holds one entry per completed and not yet confirmed exchange; those entries are removed on<br>confirmation. | 未調査 |  |
| C388 | 4.22.0→4.22.1 | パッチ | 高 | ヘッダー名/フィルタ変更 | camel-vertx-http | camel-vertx-http - the REST producer applies the outbound header filter | ヘッダー名の文字列リテラル、Constants 参照、headerFilterStrategy 設定を grep（新旧値は「Camelヘッダー値変更」シート）。外部システムとの連携ヘッダーにも注意 | camel-vertx-http, VertxHttpRestHeaderFilterStrategy.applyFilterToCamelHeaders, applyFilterToExternalHeaders, VertxHttpHeaderFilterStrategy, camel-http-common, camel-netty-http, camel-undertow, vertx-http, headerFilterStrategy, Content-Length, Content-Type, Host, Cache-Control, Connection | `VertxHttpRestHeaderFilterStrategy.applyFilterToCamelHeaders` delegated to `applyFilterToExternalHeaders`, so it consulted the inbound filter while implementing the outbound direction. The outbound filter that `VertxHttpHeaderFilterStrategy` installs was therefore never applied, and the sibling REST strategies in `camel-http-common`, `camel-netty-http` and `camel-undertow` all delegate to the matching method. A REST producer that resolves to `vertx-http` and does not configure its own `headerFil | あり | `VertxHttpRestHeaderFilterStrategy.applyFilterToCamelHeaders` delegated to<br>`applyFilterToExternalHeaders`, so it consulted the inbound filter while implementing the outbound<br>direction. The outbound filter that `VertxHttpHeaderFilterStrategy` installs was therefore never<br>applied, and the sibling REST strategies in `camel-http-common`, `camel-netty-http` and<br>`camel-undertow` all delegate to the matching method.<br><br>A REST producer that resolves to `vertx-http` and does not configure its own `headerFilterStrategy`<br>now filters the common HTTP headers on the outbound direction, as the other HTTP components already<br>did. A message header named `Content-Length`, `Content-Type`, `Host`, `Cache-Control`, `Connection`,<br>`Date`, `Pragma`, `Trailer`, `Transfer-Encoding`, `Upgrade`, `Via` or `Warning` is no longer copied<br>onto the outgoing request; the `Content-Type` of the request is still taken from the exchange as<br>before. Headers consumed by the URI template or the query parameters continue to be filtered, and a<br>custom `headerFilterStrategy` is used as-is and is unaffected.<br><br>Routes that relied on one of those headers reaching the wire must set it through the endpoint<br>configuration or supply a `headerFilterStrategy` that permits it. | 未調査 |  |
| C389 | 4.22.0→4.22.1 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-jgroups | camel-jgroups - the consumer applies a deserialization filter by default | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-jgroups, org.jgroups.Message.getObject(), java.io.ObjectInputFilter, DeserializationFilterHelper, jdk.serialFilter, java.net.**, deserializationFilter, deserializationFilter=*, ExceptionHandler, AUTH | The consumer maps an incoming cluster message to the exchange body by calling `org.jgroups.Message.getObject()`, which Java-deserializes the payload. The class of that body is now checked against a JEP-290 `java.io.ObjectInputFilter`, resolved through `DeserializationFilterHelper`. Previously no filter was applied at all, and any type a cluster peer sent was routed. When no explicit pattern is configured, the JVM-wide `jdk.serialFilter` is honoured if set, otherwise the shared Camel default allo | あり | The consumer maps an incoming cluster message to the exchange body by calling<br>`org.jgroups.Message.getObject()`, which Java-deserializes the payload. The class of that body is<br>now checked against a JEP-290 `java.io.ObjectInputFilter`, resolved through<br>`DeserializationFilterHelper`. Previously no filter was applied at all, and any type a cluster peer<br>sent was routed.<br><br>When no explicit pattern is configured, the JVM-wide `jdk.serialFilter` is honoured if set,<br>otherwise the shared Camel default allow-list is applied (it permits standard Java and Apache Camel<br>types and denies `java.net.**`). Routes that exchange their own classes over the cluster must widen<br>it through the new `deserializationFilter` endpoint option, for example:<br><br>[source,java]<br>[code]<br>    from("jgroups:clusterName?deserializationFilter=com.example.model.**;java.**;!*")<br><br>Setting `deserializationFilter=*` accepts any type and so restores the previous behavior. A refused<br>message is not routed; it is reported to the consumer's `ExceptionHandler`, which logs it at WARN<br>level by default.<br><br>Note that JGroups deserializes the payload inside its own receive path, so this check is a<br>defense-in-depth allow-list on the resulting body type. The JVM-wide `jdk.serialFilter`, together<br>with a channel secured with `AUTH` and encryption, remain the primary mitigations. | 未調査 |  |
| C390 | 4.22.0→4.22.1 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-smooks | camel-smooks - external XML entity resolution disabled by default | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-smooks, allowExternalEntities, true | The Smooks data format and the Smooks component now parse XML input with a reader that does not resolve external general or parameter entities, aligning camel-smooks with the XML parser configuration already applied by the other Camel XML components. When a Smooks configuration parses XML with the default reader, an untrusted body can no longer pull in external entities (for example `<!ENTITY x SYSTEM "file:///...">` or an `http://` reference). This only affects configurations that use the defau | あり | The Smooks data format and the Smooks component now parse XML input with a reader that does not<br>resolve external general or parameter entities, aligning camel-smooks with the XML parser<br>configuration already applied by the other Camel XML components. When a Smooks configuration parses<br>XML with the default reader, an untrusted body can no longer pull in external entities (for example<br>`<!ENTITY x SYSTEM "file:///...">` or an `http://` reference).<br><br>This only affects configurations that use the default XML reader. Configurations that declare their<br>own reader — EDI, CSV, JSON, DFDL, or a custom reader — are unchanged, and marshalling is unchanged.<br>Documents carrying an internal DTD subset still parse.<br><br>To restore the previous behaviour and allow external entity resolution, set the new<br>`allowExternalEntities` option to `true` on the data format or on the endpoint<br>(`smooks:config.xml?allowExternalEntities=true`). | 未調査 |  |
| C391 | 4.22.0→4.22.1 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-openai | camel-openai | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-openai, storeFullResponse=true, CamelOpenAIResponse, com.openai.models.chat.completions.ChatCompletion, CamelOpenAIEmbeddingsResponse, com.openai.models.embeddings.CreateEmbeddingResponse, CamelOpenAIAudioTranscriptionResponse, com.openai.models.audio.transcriptions.TranscriptionCreateResponse, CamelOpenAIAudioTranslationResponse, com.openai.models.audio.translations.TranslationCreateResponse | When `storeFullResponse=true`, the embeddings and audio operations now store their full SDK response under an operation-specific exchange property instead of the chat-completion property `CamelOpenAIResponse`. That property is typed as the chat-completion response (`com.openai.models.chat.completions.ChatCompletion`), so a downstream reader that expected that type received an incompatible object. * embeddings now use `CamelOpenAIEmbeddingsResponse` (`com.openai.models.embeddings.CreateEmbeddingR | あり | When `storeFullResponse=true`, the embeddings and audio operations now store their full SDK response<br>under an operation-specific exchange property instead of the chat-completion property `CamelOpenAIResponse`.<br>That property is typed as the chat-completion response (`com.openai.models.chat.completions.ChatCompletion`),<br>so a downstream reader that expected that type received an incompatible object.<br><br>* embeddings now use `CamelOpenAIEmbeddingsResponse` (`com.openai.models.embeddings.CreateEmbeddingResponse`).<br>* audio transcription now uses `CamelOpenAIAudioTranscriptionResponse` (`com.openai.models.audio.transcriptions.TranscriptionCreateResponse`).<br>* audio translation now uses `CamelOpenAIAudioTranslationResponse` (`com.openai.models.audio.translations.TranslationCreateResponse`).<br><br>A route that reads the full embeddings or audio response from `CamelOpenAIResponse` must switch to the<br>matching property. The chat-completion and responses operations are unchanged. | 未調査 |  |
| C392 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-lra | camel-lra - only an LRA hosted by the configured coordinator is joined | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-lra, coordinatorUrl, coordinatorContextPath, Long-Running-Action, allowedCoordinatorUrls, camel.lra.allowedCoordinatorUrls | The LRA saga service now joins, completes or compensates an LRA only when its URL is under the configured LRA coordinator (`coordinatorUrl` followed by `coordinatorContextPath`). A message whose `Long-Running-Action` header holds the URL of another coordinator now fails, instead of the saga service calling that URL. If your participants reach the same coordinator under different URLs, for example with different host names, list the other coordinator URLs, including the context path, in the new ` | あり | The LRA saga service now joins, completes or compensates an LRA only when its URL is under the configured LRA<br>coordinator (`coordinatorUrl` followed by `coordinatorContextPath`). A message whose `Long-Running-Action` header holds<br>the URL of another coordinator now fails, instead of the saga service calling that URL.<br><br>If your participants reach the same coordinator under different URLs, for example with different host names, list the<br>other coordinator URLs, including the context path, in the new `allowedCoordinatorUrls` option<br>(`camel.lra.allowedCoordinatorUrls`).<br><br>This also applies to the LRAs the service starts itself, which a nested saga route looks up again: when the<br>coordinator returns LRA URLs under another base URL than `coordinatorUrl`, for example behind a proxy, add that<br>base URL to `allowedCoordinatorUrls` as well. | 未調査 |  |
| C393 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-lra | camel-lra - warning for unsigned participant callbacks, and reserved saga option names | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-lra, callbackSecret, Camel-Saga-Compensate, Camel-Saga-Complete, Camel-Saga-Signature, Camel-Saga-Lra | The LRA saga service now logs a warning at startup when no `callbackSecret` is configured: the callbacks that the LRA coordinator sends to the participant endpoints are then not verified, so these endpoints must only be reachable by the coordinator. The Saga EIP documentation describes how to sign them. A saga option named like a parameter of the participant callback URLs, in any case (`Camel-Saga-Compensate`, `Camel-Saga-Complete`, `Camel-Saga-Signature` or `Camel-Saga-Lra`), now fails the crea | あり | The LRA saga service now logs a warning at startup when no `callbackSecret` is configured: the callbacks that the LRA<br>coordinator sends to the participant endpoints are then not verified, so these endpoints must only be reachable by the<br>coordinator. The Saga EIP documentation describes how to sign them.<br><br>A saga option named like a parameter of the participant callback URLs, in any case (`Camel-Saga-Compensate`,<br>`Camel-Saga-Complete`, `Camel-Saga-Signature` or `Camel-Saga-Lra`), now fails the creation of its route, with or<br>without a callback secret. The value of such an option could not be read back from the callback before. | 未調査 |  |
| C394 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-management | camel-management - Route group exchange counters count once per entry into the group again | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-management, ManagedRouteGroupMBean | In 4.22.1, the route group MBean (`ManagedRouteGroupMBean`) exchange counters and processing times counted each exchange once per member route instead of once per entry into the group. This was an unintended side effect of CAMEL-24590. The counters now count each exchange once per entry into the group again, as in 4.22.0: calls nested inside another route of the same group are not counted again. |  | In 4.22.1, the route group MBean (`ManagedRouteGroupMBean`) exchange counters and processing times<br>counted each exchange once per member route instead of once per entry into the group. This was an<br>unintended side effect of CAMEL-24590. The counters now count each exchange once per entry into the<br>group again, as in 4.22.0: calls nested inside another route of the same group are not counted again. | 未調査 |  |
| C395 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | (全般/その他) | Route dumps as YAML - top-level onException | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | onException, configure, RouteBuilder, camel.main.dumpRoutes=yaml, camel validate normalize, camel.main.dumpRoutesOutput | A top-level `onException` (of a YAML file, or in the `configure` method of a `RouteBuilder`) is now dumped as YAML (`camel.main.dumpRoutes=yaml`, `camel validate normalize`) once as a top-level `onException` before the routes, instead of as a step of every route, and the `onException` of a route configuration is only dumped with the route configuration, no longer in the routes. Before, such a dump did not load in the YAML DSL. When `camel.main.dumpRoutesOutput` is a file and the routes come from |  | A top-level `onException` (of a YAML file, or in the `configure` method of a `RouteBuilder`) is now dumped as YAML<br>(`camel.main.dumpRoutes=yaml`, `camel validate normalize`) once as a top-level `onException` before the routes, instead<br>of as a step of every route, and the `onException` of a route configuration is only dumped with the route<br>configuration, no longer in the routes. Before, such a dump did not load in the YAML DSL.<br><br>When `camel.main.dumpRoutesOutput` is a file and the routes come from several files, they are now dumped together, so a<br>top-level `onException` comes before the first route. When the dump is loaded, such an `onException` applies to the<br>routes of all the files, not only to those of its own file, and a WARN is logged when the routes are dumped. Dump into<br>a directory to keep one file per source file. | 未調査 |  |
| C396 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | 削除 | camel-pqc | camel-pqc - Bouncy Castle 1.86 (Breaking change) | pom/gradle の依存、URIスキーム(例: xxx:)、import、DSL要素を grep。代替先が記載されていれば置換計画を立てる | camel-pqc, BCPQC, PICNIC, signatureAlgorithm, PQCSignatureAlgorithms.PICNIC, PQCDefaultPicnicMaterial, MLDSA, SLHDSA, BC, CMCE, FRODO, FrodoKEM, mceliece348864, frodokem640 | Camel 4.22.2 uses Bouncy Castle 1.86, which removes the legacy implementations of several post-quantum algorithms from the `BCPQC` provider. *Picnic removed.* Bouncy Castle 1.86 no longer ships Picnic, so the `PICNIC` value of the `signatureAlgorithm` option, the `PQCSignatureAlgorithms.PICNIC` constant and `PQCDefaultPicnicMaterial` have been removed. Routes signing with Picnic must move to another signature algorithm, such as `MLDSA` or `SLHDSA`. *Classic McEliece and FrodoKEM use the `BC` pro |  | Camel 4.22.2 uses Bouncy Castle 1.86, which removes the legacy implementations of several post-quantum<br>algorithms from the `BCPQC` provider.<br><br>*Picnic removed.* Bouncy Castle 1.86 no longer ships Picnic, so the `PICNIC` value of the<br>`signatureAlgorithm` option, the `PQCSignatureAlgorithms.PICNIC` constant and `PQCDefaultPicnicMaterial`<br>have been removed. Routes signing with Picnic must move to another signature algorithm, such as `MLDSA`<br>or `SLHDSA`.<br><br>*Classic McEliece and FrodoKEM use the `BC` provider.* `CMCE` and `FRODO` are now served by the Classic<br>McEliece and FrodoKEM implementations of the `BC` provider (JCA names `CMCE` and `FrodoKEM`) instead of<br>`BCPQC`. That implementation has no `mceliece348864` or `frodokem640` parameter sets: the<br>`parameterSpec` option rejects them, and the default parameter sets of the key lifecycle managers changed<br>from `mceliece348864` to `mceliece460896` and from `frodokem640aes` to `frodokem976aes`.<br><br>*Stored keys must be generated again.* The `BC` provider rejects the algorithm identifier of Classic<br>McEliece and FrodoKEM keys generated by the removed `BCPQC` implementations, and Picnic keys can no<br>longer be read at all. Keys of these algorithms held by a key lifecycle manager, a key store or the<br>registry have to be regenerated, and the peers they are shared with updated.<br><br>*`parameterSpec` for `DILITHIUM`, `SPHINCSPLUS` and `KYBER`.* These algorithms generate ML-DSA, SLH-DSA<br>and ML-KEM keys, so `parameterSpec` now takes the standardized parameter-set names, for example<br>`ML-DSA-65`, `SLH-DSA-SHA2-128S` or `ML-KEM-768`. The `dilithium2`, `dilithium3` and `dilithium5` names<br>are no longer accepted, while `kyber512`, `kyber768`, `kyber1024` and SPHINCS+ names such as<br>`sha2-128s` still are. With Bouncy Castle 1.85 a `DILITHIUM` or `SPHINCSPLUS` endpoint configured with a<br>`parameterSpec` already failed to generate its key.<br><br>Code that creates key material itself has to follow the same move: the `CMCEParameterSpec`,<br>`FrodoParameterSpec`, `KyberParameterSpec`, `DilithiumParameterSpec`, `SPHINCSPlusParameterSpec` and<br>`PicnicParameterSpec` classes of `org.bouncycastle.pqc.jcajce.spec` no longer exist. Use<br>`CMCEParameterSpec`, `FrodoKEMParameterSpec`, `MLKEMParameterSpec`, `MLDSAParameterSpec` and<br>`SLHDSAParameterSpec` of `org.bouncycastle.jcajce.spec` with the `BC` provider instead. | 未調査 |  |
| C397 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-pqc | camel-pqc - a configured KeyGenerator or KeyAgreement is used by one exchange at a time | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-pqc, pqc, KeyGenerator, KeyAgreement, init, getKeyGenerator(), CamelPQCKemAlgorithm | When Camel creates the instance itself, the KEM operations of the `pqc` component (including the hybrid KEM operations) and the PQC data format now use a new `KeyGenerator`, and for the hybrid operations a new `KeyAgreement`, for every operation. A configured instance is still shared: a registry bean, which is autowired into every `pqc` endpoint, a `KeyGenerator` set on the data format, or the default material used when no key material is configured. Each operation now holds its lock from `init` |  | When Camel creates the instance itself, the KEM operations of the `pqc` component (including the hybrid KEM<br>operations) and the PQC data format now use a new `KeyGenerator`, and for the hybrid operations a new `KeyAgreement`,<br>for every operation. A configured instance is still shared: a registry bean, which is autowired into every `pqc`<br>endpoint, a `KeyGenerator` set on the data format, or the default material used when no key material is configured.<br>Each operation now holds its lock from `init` until the result is returned, so concurrent exchanges that use it run<br>one at a time.<br><br>A started PQC data format no longer keeps a `KeyGenerator` of its own: `getKeyGenerator()` returns only a configured<br>instance and, unless one is configured, the `CamelPQCKemAlgorithm` header now selects the KEM algorithm of each<br>operation. | 未調査 |  |
| C398 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-netty-http | camel-netty-http - the roles of a security constraint are matched by role name | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-netty-http, SecurityConstraintMapping, admin guest, admin,guest | The roles of a `SecurityConstraintMapping` inclusion are a comma-separated list of role names, and an authenticated user is now accepted only when one of their roles is equal to one of those names. The comparison is case-sensitive, whitespace around each name and blank entries are ignored, and a value of `*` still accepts any role. A roles value that uses another separator, such as `admin;guest` or `admin guest`, must be changed to `admin,guest`. | あり | The roles of a `SecurityConstraintMapping` inclusion are a comma-separated list of role names, and an authenticated<br>user is now accepted only when one of their roles is equal to one of those names. The comparison is case-sensitive,<br>whitespace around each name and blank entries are ignored, and a value of `*` still accepts any role. A roles value<br>that uses another separator, such as `admin;guest` or `admin guest`, must be changed to `admin,guest`. | 未調査 |  |
| C399 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-graphql | camel-graphql - the credentials are only sent to the authority of httpUri | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-graphql, accessToken, jwtAuthorizationType, username, password, proxyHost, CamelHttpUri, CamelHttpPath, CamelHttpQuery, CamelHttpMethod, CamelHttpProtocolVersion | The `accessToken` (with its `jwtAuthorizationType`) is now added to a request only when the request goes to the scheme, host and port of `httpUri`, and the `username` and `password` are registered for that authority only. Previously neither was bound to the authority of `httpUri`. A request to another authority, including the same host with another scheme or port, is now sent without them. A route that needs to authenticate to another authority must address it in `httpUri`. When `proxyHost` is s | あり | The `accessToken` (with its `jwtAuthorizationType`) is now added to a request only when the request goes to the<br>scheme, host and port of `httpUri`, and the `username` and `password` are registered for that authority only.<br>Previously neither was bound to the authority of `httpUri`. A request to another authority, including the same host<br>with another scheme or port, is now sent without them. A route that needs to authenticate to another authority must<br>address it in `httpUri`. When `proxyHost` is set, the `username` and `password` are no longer offered to the proxy when<br>it asks for authentication.<br><br>The producer also no longer takes the request URL from the `CamelHttpUri`, `CamelHttpPath`, `CamelHttpQuery` and other<br>camel-http control headers of the message. It did so since Camel 4.19, when the component moved onto camel-http; the<br>request now always goes to `httpUri`, as it did before. For the same reason the `CamelHttpMethod` and<br>`CamelHttpProtocolVersion` headers no longer apply, and the request is always a POST. | 未調査 |  |
| C400 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-telegram | camel-telegram - webhook requests are verified with a secret token | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-telegram, X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token, webhookSecretToken, webhookAutoRegister=true, WebhookRoutePolicy, secret_token, setWebhook, webhookPath, webhookSecretTokenEnabled=false | In webhook mode, Camel now registers the webhook with a secret token, which Telegram sends in the `X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token` header of every webhook request, and rejects a webhook request that does not carry the token with HTTP 403. The token is the value of the new `webhookSecretToken` option or, when that option is not set, a value derived from the authorization token. A client that calls the webhook endpoint directly, for example in a test, must send the header too. When Camel register | あり | In webhook mode, Camel now registers the webhook with a secret token, which Telegram sends in the<br>`X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token` header of every webhook request, and rejects a webhook request that does not carry<br>the token with HTTP 403. The token is the value of the new `webhookSecretToken` option or, when that option is not<br>set, a value derived from the authorization token. A client that calls the webhook endpoint directly, for example in<br>a test, must send the header too.<br><br>When Camel registers the webhook at startup (`webhookAutoRegister=true`, the default), nothing needs to change: each<br>upgraded instance registers the webhook with the token, and the instances that are not upgraded yet ignore the header.<br><br>When the webhook is registered in another way, through the `WebhookRoutePolicy` or outside Camel, the registration<br>made with the previous version has no secret token, and the upgraded instances reject every update until the webhook<br>is registered again with it. Register the webhook again first, then upgrade the instances that receive the updates:<br>instances of the previous version ignore the header. With the `WebhookRoutePolicy`, run the registration with the new<br>version. Outside Camel, set `webhookSecretToken`, and pass the same value as the `secret_token` parameter of<br>`setWebhook`.<br><br>The default webhook path is a hash of the endpoint URI, so adding an option to the URI, such as `webhookSecretToken`,<br>changes the path. When the webhook is not registered by Camel at startup, set `webhookPath` to keep the path that is<br>registered.<br><br>To restore the previous behaviour, set `webhookSecretTokenEnabled=false`: the webhook is then registered without a<br>secret token, and webhook requests are not verified. | 未調査 |  |
| C401 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | ヘッダー名/フィルタ変更 | camel-azure-eventhubs | camel-azure-eventhubs | ヘッダー名の文字列リテラル、Constants 参照、headerFilterStrategy 設定を grep（新旧値は「Camelヘッダー値変更」シート）。外部システムとの連携ヘッダーにも注意 | camel-azure-eventhubs, Camel*, EventData, headerFilterStrategy, CamelAzureEventHubsPartitionKey, CamelAzureEventHubsPartitionId, Both partitionKey and partitionId are set, partitionKey, partitionId, CamelAzureEventHubsReceivedPartitionId | The producer now leaves the Camel-internal headers (`Camel*`) out of the `EventData` application properties by default. The 4.22.0 upgrade guide already announced this, but the filter was not installed, so 4.22.0 and 4.22.1 still copied every header. Configure a custom `headerFilterStrategy` on the component to change which headers are sent. A route that consumes from one Event Hub and produces to another no longer fails, or ignores the producer configuration, because of the `CamelAzureEventHubs | あり | The producer now leaves the Camel-internal headers (`Camel*`) out of the `EventData` application properties by<br>default. The 4.22.0 upgrade guide already announced this, but the filter was not installed, so 4.22.0 and 4.22.1 still<br>copied every header. Configure a custom `headerFilterStrategy` on the component<br>to change which headers are sent.<br><br>A route that consumes from one Event Hub and produces to another no longer fails, or ignores the producer<br>configuration, because of the `CamelAzureEventHubsPartitionKey` and `CamelAzureEventHubsPartitionId` headers that the<br>consumer sets. Such a route used to fail with `Both partitionKey and partitionId are set` for every event with a<br>partition key, and for every event when `partitionKey` was configured, and a configured `partitionId` was replaced by<br>the partition the event was received from. The producer now picks the partition from, in this order: a partition<br>header set by the route, the `partitionKey` or `partitionId` endpoint option, and the partition key of the received<br>event. It no longer reuses the partition id of the received event, so an event without a partition key is no longer<br>sent to the partition with the same id in the target Event Hub. To keep doing so, for example when mirroring between<br>Event Hubs that have the same partitions, remove the `CamelAzureEventHubsReceivedPartitionId` exchange property before<br>the producer. | 未調査 |  |
| C402 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-xslt, camel-xslt-saxon | camel-xslt and camel-xslt-saxon - implicit DOM sources | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-xslt, camel-xslt-saxon, Source, DOMSource, match="/", xslt:, source, DOMSource(element) | When a non-`Source` input is implicitly converted to a `DOMSource` pointing at its owner document's root element, the Saxon-backed XSLT transformer now starts at the document node. This preserves document-root (`match="/"`) template behavior when, for example, a CXF payload is converted to a DOM source. The default JDK XSLT transformer already starts at the document node; the change also applies to `xslt:` when configured with Saxon as its transformer factory. The original DOM and source system |  | When a non-`Source` input is implicitly converted to a `DOMSource` pointing at its owner document's<br>root element, the Saxon-backed XSLT transformer now starts at the document node. This preserves<br>document-root (`match="/"`) template behavior when, for example, a CXF payload is converted to a DOM<br>source. The default JDK XSLT transformer already starts at the document node; the change also applies<br>to `xslt:` when configured with Saxon as its transformer factory.<br>The original DOM and source system ID are preserved. Nested and detached elements are unchanged.<br>Explicit `Source` inputs, including a `Source` returned by the endpoint's `source` expression,<br>retain their selected context node, and streaming sources are unchanged.<br><br>Custom implicit converters that intentionally select the document element as the XSLT context<br>may observe different template selection. To retain element-context semantics, provide an explicit<br>`DOMSource(element)` as the body or through the endpoint's `source` expression. | 未調査 |  |
| C403 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-mina | camel-mina - the host name of the server is verified over SSL | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-mina, sslContextParameters, useGlobalSslContextParameters, clientMode=true, host, hostnameVerification, false, writeTimeout, timeout, ERROR, org.apache.mina.filter.ssl.SslHandler | When `sslContextParameters` is set (on the endpoint, or with `useGlobalSslContextParameters` on the component), the producer, and the consumer with `clientMode=true`, now check that the certificate of the server matches the `host` of the endpoint, with the same rules as an HTTPS client. Before, any certificate trusted by the trust store was accepted, whatever host the certificate was issued for. A connection to a host name or an IP address that the certificate does not list now fails the SSL han | あり | When `sslContextParameters` is set (on the endpoint, or with `useGlobalSslContextParameters` on the component), the<br>producer, and the consumer with `clientMode=true`, now check that the certificate of the server matches the `host` of<br>the endpoint, with the same rules as an HTTPS client. Before, any certificate trusted by the trust store was accepted,<br>whatever host the certificate was issued for.<br><br>A connection to a host name or an IP address that the certificate does not list now fails the SSL handshake; an IP<br>address must be listed as a subject alternative name of the certificate. Use a certificate that matches the host of the<br>endpoint, or set the new `hostnameVerification` option to `false` to keep the previous behaviour.<br><br>MINA does not pass a failed handshake on as an error: the producer fails with a timeout (after `writeTimeout`, or<br>`timeout` while waiting for a reply), and the handshake error is logged at `ERROR` level by<br>`org.apache.mina.filter.ssl.SslHandler`. A producer that starts timing out after the upgrade should be checked for a<br>certificate that does not list the host. | 未調査 |  |
| C404 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-mllp | camel-mllp - the producer verifies the host name of the server over TLS | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-mllp, sslContextParameters, useGlobalSslContextParameters, mllp://8888, hostnameVerification, false | When `sslContextParameters` is set (on the endpoint, or with `useGlobalSslContextParameters` on the component), the MLLP producer now checks that the certificate of the server matches the host it connects to, with the same rules as an HTTPS client. Before, it accepted any certificate trusted by the trust store, whatever host the certificate was issued for. A producer that connects with a host name or an IP address that the certificate does not list now fails the TLS handshake; an IP address must | あり | When `sslContextParameters` is set (on the endpoint, or with `useGlobalSslContextParameters` on the component), the<br>MLLP producer now checks that the certificate of the server matches the host it connects to, with the same rules as an<br>HTTPS client. Before, it accepted any certificate trusted by the trust store, whatever host the certificate was issued<br>for.<br><br>A producer that connects with a host name or an IP address that the certificate does not list now fails the TLS<br>handshake; an IP address must be listed as a subject alternative name of the certificate, and a producer URI without a<br>host name (such as `mllp://8888`) cannot pass the check. Use a certificate that matches the host of the endpoint, or set<br>the new `hostnameVerification` option to `false` to keep the previous behaviour. | 未調査 |  |
| C405 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-smpp | camel-smpp - the host name of the SMSC is verified over SSL | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-smpp, smpps, usingSSL=true, hostnameVerification, false, IOException | With `smpps` (or `usingSSL=true`), directly or through an HTTP proxy, the connection now checks that the certificate of the SMSC matches the host it connects to, with the same rules as an HTTPS client. Before, any certificate trusted by the JVM was accepted, whatever host it was issued for. A connection to a host name or an IP address that the certificate does not list now fails the SSL handshake; an IP address must be listed as a subject alternative name of the certificate. Use a certificate th | あり | With `smpps` (or `usingSSL=true`), directly or through an HTTP proxy, the connection now checks that the certificate of<br>the SMSC matches the host it connects to, with the same rules as an HTTPS client. Before, any certificate trusted by the<br>JVM was accepted, whatever host it was issued for.<br><br>A connection to a host name or an IP address that the certificate does not list now fails the SSL handshake; an IP<br>address must be listed as a subject alternative name of the certificate. Use a certificate that matches the host of the<br>endpoint, or set the new `hostnameVerification` option to `false` to keep the previous behaviour.<br><br>A mismatch shows as the producer or consumer failing to start, with an `IOException` whose cause names the host that<br>was checked:<br><br>[source]<br>[code]<br>    java.io.IOException: No subject alternative names matching IP address 127.0.0.1 found<br>        Caused by: javax.net.ssl.SSLHandshakeException: No subject alternative names matching IP address 127.0.0.1 found | 未調査 |  |
| C406 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-zipfile, camel-tarfile | camel-zipfile, camel-tarfile - a maxDecompressedSize of 2 GiB or more is now enforced | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-zipfile, camel-tarfile, maxDecompressedSize, ZipSplitter, Integer.MAX_VALUE, IOException, -1, IOHelper.copy(InputStream, OutputStream, int, boolean, long) | The `maxDecompressedSize` option of the Zip File and Tar File data formats (and of `ZipSplitter`) was not enforced when set to 2 GiB (`Integer.MAX_VALUE` bytes) or more, because the byte count behind the check wrapped around. The limit is now enforced for any value: unmarshalling an entry that decompresses to more than the configured `maxDecompressedSize` fails with an `IOException`, as documented. The default limit (1 GiB) is unchanged, and `-1` still disables the limit. `IOHelper.copy(InputStr | あり | The `maxDecompressedSize` option of the Zip File and Tar File data formats (and of `ZipSplitter`) was not<br>enforced when set to 2 GiB (`Integer.MAX_VALUE` bytes) or more, because the byte count behind the check<br>wrapped around. The limit is now enforced for any value: unmarshalling an entry that decompresses to more<br>than the configured `maxDecompressedSize` fails with an `IOException`, as documented. The default limit<br>(1 GiB) is unchanged, and `-1` still disables the limit.<br><br>`IOHelper.copy(InputStream, OutputStream, int, boolean, long)` now returns `Integer.MAX_VALUE`, instead of a<br>negative number, when it copies more than `Integer.MAX_VALUE` bytes. | 未調査 |  |
| C407 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-oauth | camel-oauth - the bearer token processor is stateless and reads the HTTP request headers | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-oauth, OAuthBearerTokenProcessor, camel.oauth.session, CamelOAuthSessionId, UserProfile, CamelOAuthUserProfile, OAuth.CAMEL_OAUTH_USER_PROFILE, Authorization, Cookie, OAuthHelper.validateOAuthToken | `OAuthBearerTokenProcessor` no longer creates or updates the OAuth session, and no longer sets the `camel.oauth.session` cookie nor the `CamelOAuthSessionId` header: a bearer token authenticates the request that carries it, and nothing else. The authenticated `UserProfile` is available in the `CamelOAuthUserProfile` exchange property (`OAuth.CAMEL_OAUTH_USER_PROFILE`). A route that read the profile from the OAuth session after `OAuthBearerTokenProcessor` must read it from that exchange property | あり | `OAuthBearerTokenProcessor` no longer creates or updates the OAuth session, and no longer sets the<br>`camel.oauth.session` cookie nor the `CamelOAuthSessionId` header: a bearer token authenticates the request that<br>carries it, and nothing else. The authenticated `UserProfile` is available in the `CamelOAuthUserProfile` exchange<br>property (`OAuth.CAMEL_OAUTH_USER_PROFILE`). A route that read the profile from the OAuth session after<br>`OAuthBearerTokenProcessor` must read it from that exchange property instead.<br><br>When the message comes from platform-http (on Vert.x or on Spring Boot), from a servlet based HTTP consumer<br>(camel-servlet, camel-jetty) or from camel-netty-http, the bearer token and the session cookie are now read from the<br>`Authorization` and `Cookie` headers of the HTTP request only. A query or form parameter of the same name, which these<br>consumers also map into the message headers, is no longer used for them, and neither is an `Authorization` or `Cookie`<br>message header that the route sets itself. For example<br>`+.setHeader("Authorization", simple("Bearer ${header.X-Forwarded-Access-Token}"))+` before<br>`OAuthBearerTokenProcessor` now results in a 401 response. A route that takes the token from elsewhere can validate it<br>with `OAuthHelper.validateOAuthToken` from camel-support instead.<br><br>For any other message, such as one from camel-undertow, the processors keep reading the message headers, but leave out<br>a value that also appears in the query string of the request. | 未調査 |  |
| C408 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-oauth | camel-oauth - the post login url is confined to the configured redirect uri origin | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-oauth, scheme://host[:port], camel.oauth.redirect-uri, OAuthCodeFlowProcessor, X-Forwarded-Proto, X-Forwarded-Host, X-Forwarded-Port, Host, CamelHttpUrl | The post login url of the authorization code flow is now always built from the origin (`scheme://host[:port]`) of the configured `camel.oauth.redirect-uri`, plus the requested path. `OAuthCodeFlowProcessor` previously rebuilt that url from the `X-Forwarded-Proto` / `X-Forwarded-Host` / `X-Forwarded-Port` request headers, or from the `Host` header behind `CamelHttpUrl` when those were absent. All of those are set by the caller, so a request could point the post login redirect at any origin. A dep | あり | The post login url of the authorization code flow is now always built from the origin (`scheme://host[:port]`)<br>of the configured `camel.oauth.redirect-uri`, plus the requested path. `OAuthCodeFlowProcessor` previously<br>rebuilt that url from the `X-Forwarded-Proto` / `X-Forwarded-Host` / `X-Forwarded-Port` request headers, or<br>from the `Host` header behind `CamelHttpUrl` when those were absent. All of those are set by the caller, so<br>a request could point the post login redirect at any origin. A deployment behind an ingress or an OpenShift<br>Route still redirects to its externally reachable address, because `camel.oauth.redirect-uri` is the address<br>the identity provider sends the browser back to. Deployments whose external address differs from that<br>property must set it to the address the browser actually reaches; a request announcing another origin is now<br>redirected to the configured one and a warning is logged. | 未調査 |  |
