| C412 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-http-common, camel-platform-http-vertx | camel-http-common, camel-platform-http-vertx - fileNameExtWhitelist entries are matched exactly | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-http-common, camel-platform-http-vertx, fileNameExtWhitelist, camel-http-base, txt, evil.x, camel-platform-http-vertx, DefaultHttpBinding, camel-http-common | `fileNameExtWhitelist` is now checked the same way everywhere, by one shared check in `camel-http-base`. Two places still matched each extension as a substring of the whitelist, so for example a whitelist of `txt` accepted an upload named `evil.x`: the `camel-platform-http-vertx` consumer, and `DefaultHttpBinding` in `camel-http-common` for uploads that arrive as request attributes, which also replaced the configured `fileNameExtWhitelist` with its lower-cased value. Both now compare each comma- | あり | `fileNameExtWhitelist` is now checked the same way everywhere, by one shared check in `camel-http-base`. Two<br>places still matched each extension as a substring of the whitelist, so for example a whitelist of `txt`<br>accepted an upload named `evil.x`: the `camel-platform-http-vertx` consumer, and `DefaultHttpBinding` in<br>`camel-http-common` for uploads that arrive as request attributes, which also replaced the configured<br>`fileNameExtWhitelist` with its lower-cased value. Both now compare each comma-separated entry exactly and<br>case-insensitively. `*` still accepts every file, a file name without an extension is still accepted, and the<br>configured value is left unchanged. An upload whose extension only matched as part of a longer entry is now<br>rejected. | 未調査 |  |
| C413 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-core | camel-core - masking of sensitive values in endpoint URIs | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-core, URISupport.sanitizeUri(), access-key, accessKey, RAW(...), RAW{...}, Unknown parameters=[...], camel.main.additionalSensitiveKeywords, URISupport.addSanitizeKeywords(), SensitiveUtils.maskUserInfoCredentials(),  before the path, so a password may contain , , and an | `URISupport.sanitizeUri()`, which masks secrets in endpoint URIs shown in logs, events, JMX names and error messages, now masks some values it used to miss, so the masked form of a URI can differ from earlier releases: * option names are matched ignoring dashes, so `access-key` is masked like `accessKey` * a `RAW(...)` or `RAW{...}` value is masked up to the bracket that ends it, also when the value contains that bracket * the userinfo password of every URI in a text is masked, not only the last | あり | `URISupport.sanitizeUri()`, which masks secrets in endpoint URIs shown in logs, events, JMX names and error<br>messages, now masks some values it used to miss, so the masked form of a URI can differ from earlier releases:<br><br>* option names are matched ignoring dashes, so `access-key` is masked like `accessKey`<br>* a `RAW(...)` or `RAW{...}` value is masked up to the bracket that ends it, also when the value contains that bracket<br>* the userinfo password of every URI in a text is masked, not only the last one<br>* the `Unknown parameters=[...]` message of an endpoint that cannot be created masks the values of sensitive parameters<br><br>The keywords added with `camel.main.additionalSensitiveKeywords` (or `URISupport.addSanitizeKeywords()`) now apply to<br>every matching parameter, not only the first one, and they are added to the keywords configured earlier instead of<br>replacing them. The keywords apply to the whole JVM and cannot be removed.<br><br>`SensitiveUtils.maskUserInfoCredentials()`, used when masking log messages, uses the same userinfo rule: the userinfo<br>ends at the last `@` before the path, so a password may contain `@`, and an `@` in the query of a URI is no longer<br>taken as the end of a password. | 未調査 |  |
| C414 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-core | camel-core - Rest DSL response Content-Type | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-core, produces, application/json, application/xml, text/plain, */* | Under json or xml binding, a response without a Content-Type header again takes it from the `produces` of the rest verb, as before Camel 4.18.4 and 4.22.0. Those releases used `application/json` (or `application/xml`) whenever the binding mode allowed it and marshalled the body, so a verb producing `text/plain` answered with a json-quoted body and a binary body failed. When `produces` lists several media types, the first json (or xml) type is used, otherwise the first one. Wildcards such as `*/* | あり | Under json or xml binding, a response without a Content-Type header again takes it from the `produces` of the rest<br>verb, as before Camel 4.18.4 and 4.22.0. Those releases used `application/json` (or `application/xml`) whenever the<br>binding mode allowed it and marshalled the body, so a verb producing `text/plain` answered with a json-quoted body and<br>a binary body failed. When `produces` lists several media types, the first json (or xml) type is used, otherwise the<br>first one. Wildcards such as `*/*` are skipped, falling back to `application/json` or `application/xml`. | 未調査 |  |
| C415 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | 破壊的変更(要確認) | camel-mustache, camel-chunk | camel-mustache, camel-chunk - potential breaking change | 原文全文を読み、該当するオプション/クラス/ヘッダー/URI を grep。使用していれば修正が必要 | camel-mustache, camel-chunk, MustacheConstants, ChunkConstants, DefaultHeaderFilterStrategy, MustacheConstants.MUSTACHE_RESOURCE_URI, MustacheResourceUri, CamelMustacheResourceUri, MustacheConstants.MUSTACHE_TEMPLATE, MustacheTemplate, CamelMustacheTemplate, ChunkConstants.CHUNK_RESOURCE_URI, ChunkResourceUri, CamelChunkResourceUri | The Exchange header constants in `MustacheConstants` and `ChunkConstants` have been renamed to follow the Camel naming convention used across the rest of the component catalog (so that they are handled consistently by `DefaultHeaderFilterStrategy`, like the other template components). The Java field names are unchanged; only the header string values have changed. `MustacheConstants`: \| Constant \| Previous value \| New value \| `MustacheConstants.MUSTACHE_RESOURCE_URI` \| `MustacheResourceUri` \| `Ca | あり | The Exchange header constants in `MustacheConstants` and `ChunkConstants` have been renamed to<br>follow the Camel naming convention used across the rest of the component catalog (so that they are<br>handled consistently by `DefaultHeaderFilterStrategy`, like the other template components). The Java<br>field names are unchanged; only the header string values have changed.<br><br>`MustacheConstants`:<br><br>[options="header"]<br>\|===<br>\| Constant \| Previous value \| New value<br>\| `MustacheConstants.MUSTACHE_RESOURCE_URI` \| `MustacheResourceUri` \| `CamelMustacheResourceUri`<br>\| `MustacheConstants.MUSTACHE_TEMPLATE` \| `MustacheTemplate` \| `CamelMustacheTemplate`<br>\|===<br><br>`ChunkConstants`:<br><br>[options="header"]<br>\|===<br>\| Constant \| Previous value \| New value<br>\| `ChunkConstants.CHUNK_RESOURCE_URI` \| `ChunkResourceUri` \| `CamelChunkResourceUri`<br>\| `ChunkConstants.CHUNK_TEMPLATE` \| `ChunkTemplate` \| `CamelChunkTemplate`<br>\|===<br><br>Both components read these headers only when `allowTemplateFromHeader=true`. Because the old names sat<br>outside the `Camel` namespace, `DefaultHeaderFilterStrategy` did not strip them, so such a header<br>arriving from an untrusted sender reached the producer; with the `Camel` prefix the headers are now<br>filtered at the component boundary, so the template or resource can only come from the route. For that<br>reason the old names should not simply be restored.<br><br>Routes that reference the constants (for example `setHeader(MustacheConstants.MUSTACHE_TEMPLATE, ...)`)<br>are unaffected. Routes that set the header by its literal string name, or that use<br>`allowTemplateFromHeader=true` with the old header names, must switch to the new `Camel`-prefixed<br>names. | 未調査 |  |
| C416 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-chunk | camel-chunk - message data printed with a direct tag is rendered literally | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-chunk, chunk, {$headers.name}, {$tag}, slice, get, join, List, Collection, Set, {$body}, toString(), {$body.name}, {$exception.message} | Previously the `chunk` component bound the message body, headers and variables into the Chunk engine so that Chunk re-parsed those values as template source: a value that itself contained Chunk tags (such as a body of `{$headers.name}`) had those tags expanded instead of being printed verbatim. Message data bound to the engine is now neutralised so that a direct `{$tag}` printing the body, a header, a variable, or an element of a nested map, list or array renders the value literally instead of e | あり | Previously the `chunk` component bound the message body, headers and variables into the Chunk engine so that<br>Chunk re-parsed those values as template source: a value that itself contained Chunk tags (such as a body of<br>`{$headers.name}`) had those tags expanded instead of being printed verbatim.<br><br>Message data bound to the engine is now neutralised so that a direct `{$tag}` printing the body, a header, a<br>variable, or an element of a nested map, list or array renders the value literally instead of evaluating the<br>tags inside it. Tag-free data is unchanged and Chunk's string filters (for example `slice`, `get`, `join`)<br>keep their existing behaviour. Routes that relied on message data being evaluated as Chunk template code must<br>move that markup into the template itself.<br><br>As part of this, a non-`List` `Collection` value (such as a `Set`) is now bound as a `List`, so a direct<br>`{$body}` prints Chunk's list placeholder instead of the collection's `toString()`, and a filter such as<br>`\|join` operates on its elements.<br><br>This does not cover every path: Chunk re-parses any string it produces while rendering, so the output of a<br>filter (`{$body\|trim}`), a string property of a bean body (`{$body.name}`, `{$exception.message}`) and string<br>items bound by a `{% loop %}` are still parsed as template code. Keep untrusted data to direct `{$tag}`<br>output; do not pass untrusted values through Chunk filters, bean properties or loops. If untrusted data must<br>go through one of those paths, remove the `{` and `}` characters from it in the route before the `chunk`<br>endpoint (Chunk has no escape for tags inside data), for example with a processor that rewrites the body or<br>header. | 未調査 |  |
| C417 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-debezium | camel-debezium - a failed embedded engine is now reported | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-debezium, CompletionCallback, ExceptionHandler, DOWN, UP | The Debezium consumers now register a `CompletionCallback` on the embedded engine. When the engine stops with an error - for example because the connector cannot reach the database, or the offset store cannot be read - the failure is passed to the consumer's `ExceptionHandler`, and the consumer's health check reports `DOWN` with that error. Previously the engine reported such failures only through its own logger, so the route stayed started and healthy while no longer receiving any change event. |  | The Debezium consumers now register a `CompletionCallback` on the embedded engine. When the engine stops<br>with an error - for example because the connector cannot reach the database, or the offset store cannot be<br>read - the failure is passed to the consumer's `ExceptionHandler`, and the consumer's health check reports<br>`DOWN` with that error.<br><br>Previously the engine reported such failures only through its own logger, so the route stayed started and<br>healthy while no longer receiving any change event. Deployments that use readiness or liveness probes will<br>now see a Debezium route whose engine has died reported as `DOWN`, where it was previously reported as `UP`.<br>The engine is still not restarted automatically. | 未調査 |  |
| C418 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-saga | camel-saga | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-saga, saga:complete, saga:compensate, Long-Running-Action, CamelSagaService, true, isLongRunningActionHeaderSupported(), LRASagaService, InMemorySagaService, IllegalStateException, exchange.getExchangeExtension().setSagaLongRunningAction(id) | The `saga:complete` and `saga:compensate` endpoints now follow the same rule as the Saga EIP: when the exchange is not bound to a saga, the `Long-Running-Action` message header is consulted only if the configured `CamelSagaService` returns `true` from `isLongRunningActionHeaderSupported()`, as `LRASagaService` does. With the default `InMemorySagaService` the header is ignored, and sending an exchange that is not bound to a saga to these endpoints fails with `IllegalStateException`. Exchanges cre | あり | The `saga:complete` and `saga:compensate` endpoints now follow the same rule as the Saga EIP: when the<br>exchange is not bound to a saga, the `Long-Running-Action` message header is consulted only if the<br>configured `CamelSagaService` returns `true` from `isLongRunningActionHeaderSupported()`, as<br>`LRASagaService` does. With the default `InMemorySagaService` the header is ignored, and sending an<br>exchange that is not bound to a saga to these endpoints fails with `IllegalStateException`.<br><br>Exchanges created inside a saga, including copies made by EIPs such as Wire Tap, Multicast or SEDA,<br>stay bound to it and are not affected. A route that completes or compensates an in-memory saga from an<br>unrelated exchange must bind it explicitly from trusted code, for example with<br>`exchange.getExchangeExtension().setSagaLongRunningAction(id)`. | 未調査 |  |
| C419 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-coap | camel-coap | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-coap, 5.00 Internal Server Error, 2.05 Content, byte[], muteException, true, camel-knative, camel-mina, camel-cxf, camel-grpc, restConfiguration().endpointProperty("muteException", "false") | The CoAP consumer now answers a failed exchange with `5.00 Internal Server Error`, and no longer returns the exception's message to the client. Previously the consumer did not check whether the exchange had failed: a route failure was answered with `2.05 Content` and whatever body the message held when the route failed. When the response could not be built once the route had completed, for example because the body could not be converted to `byte[]`, the exception's message was sent to the client | あり | The CoAP consumer now answers a failed exchange with `5.00 Internal Server Error`, and no longer returns<br>the exception's message to the client.<br><br>Previously the consumer did not check whether the exchange had failed: a route failure was answered with<br>`2.05 Content` and whatever body the message held when the route failed. When the response could not be<br>built once the route had completed, for example because the body could not be converted to `byte[]`, the<br>exception's message was sent to the client as the payload of a `5.00 Internal Server Error` response.<br><br>A new `muteException` consumer option controls the payload of the error response, and it defaults to<br>`true`, the same default as the HTTP consumers and the `camel-knative`, `camel-mina`, `camel-cxf` and<br>`camel-grpc` consumers: the payload is empty. A route that relies on the exception's message reaching the<br>client must opt back in explicitly:<br><br>[source,text]<br>[code]<br>    coap://0.0.0.0:5683/my/resource?muteException=false<br><br>For the Rest DSL, set it with `restConfiguration().endpointProperty("muteException", "false")`. | 未調査 |  |
| C420 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-docling | camel-docling - output path handling | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-docling, CamelDoclingOutputFilePath, .., outputBaseDirectory, inputBaseDirectory, IOException | The `CamelDoclingOutputFilePath` header, which selects the CLI output directory, is now normalized lexically (redundant separators and `.`/`..` segments are resolved) before it is passed to Docling; a header value without such segments is still used as given. A new `outputBaseDirectory` option additionally confines the header the same way `inputBaseDirectory` confines input paths - when set, an output path that resolves outside it, including an absolute path, is rejected with an `IOException`. ` |  | The `CamelDoclingOutputFilePath` header, which selects the CLI output directory, is now normalized lexically<br>(redundant separators and `.`/`..` segments are resolved) before it is passed to Docling; a header value<br>without such segments is still used as given. A new `outputBaseDirectory` option additionally confines the<br>header the same way `inputBaseDirectory` confines input paths - when set, an output path that resolves outside<br>it, including an absolute path, is rejected with an `IOException`. `outputBaseDirectory` is unset by default. | 未調査 |  |
| C421 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-undertow | camel-undertow - WebSocket endpoints apply the security provider, allowed roles and handlers | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-undertow, ws://, wss://, UndertowSecurityProvider, securityConfiguration, securityProvider, allowedRoles, handlers, accessLog, 403, oauthProfile | WebSocket endpoints (`ws://` and `wss://`) now apply the `UndertowSecurityProvider` (the `securityConfiguration` or `securityProvider` option), the `allowedRoles` option, and the `handlers` and `accessLog` options, as HTTP endpoints do. Previously these options had no effect on WebSocket endpoints. They apply to the upgrade request: a client that the security provider rejects, or that connects to an endpoint with `allowedRoles` but no security provider, now gets the same status code as on an HTT | あり | WebSocket endpoints (`ws://` and `wss://`) now apply the `UndertowSecurityProvider` (the `securityConfiguration` or<br>`securityProvider` option), the `allowedRoles` option, and the `handlers` and `accessLog` options, as HTTP endpoints<br>do. Previously these options had no effect on WebSocket endpoints. They apply to the upgrade request: a client that<br>the security provider rejects, or that connects to an endpoint with `allowedRoles` but no security provider, now gets<br>the same status code as on an HTTP endpoint (for example `403`) and no connection is opened. The headers that the<br>security provider adds are set on the exchanges of the connection.<br><br>All the endpoints of a WebSocket path share its connections. The settings of the consumer apply to the path,<br>including the messages sent by producers on that path, and keep applying while the consumer is stopped; a path that<br>only has producers applies their settings. This also applies to the `oauthProfile` option: while the consumer is<br>stopped, upgrade requests to its path are still validated. A connection that was opened before these settings<br>applied does not receive the messages of the producers, and it is closed when it sends a message.<br><br>A WebSocket client that connected without satisfying the configured security provider or allowed roles is now<br>rejected: it must authenticate, or the option must be removed from the WebSocket endpoint. | 未調査 |  |
| C422 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-crypto | camel-crypto | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-crypto, CryptoDataFormat, marshal, shouldInlineInitializationVector, CamelCryptoInitVector, Given final block not properly padded, Message authentication failed, HMAC_k | Three changes to `CryptoDataFormat`, none of which affects the format of data already written. *A per-message initialization vector when inlining.* `marshal` used to throw `Inlining cannot be performed, as no initialization vector was specified` when `shouldInlineInitializationVector` was set without a statically configured vector — which pushed routes into reusing one vector for every message, the thing inlining exists to avoid. A fresh vector is now generated per message when none is supplied. |  | Three changes to `CryptoDataFormat`, none of which affects the format of data already written.<br><br>*A per-message initialization vector when inlining.* `marshal` used to throw<br>`Inlining cannot be performed, as no initialization vector was specified` when<br>`shouldInlineInitializationVector` was set without a statically configured vector — which pushed routes<br>into reusing one vector for every message, the thing inlining exists to avoid. A fresh vector is now<br>generated per message when none is supplied. Because the vector is written into the message, readers pick<br>it up from the stream and need no change. A vector supplied explicitly, by configuration or by the<br>`CamelCryptoInitVector` header, is still used as given.<br><br>*Authentication failures report uniformly.* A tampered message previously surfaced two distinguishable<br>outcomes: `Given final block not properly padded` from the cipher, or `Expected mac did not match actual<br>mac` from the MAC check. A caller able to submit ciphertext and observe which one came back can use that<br>distinction to recover plaintext. Both now report `Message authentication failed`, and the message no<br>longer includes the expected and computed MAC values — the computed one is `HMAC_k` over the plaintext<br>just produced. Code matching on the old text must be updated.<br><br>*The inlined vector length is bounded.* The length prefix is read from the message and used to size an<br>allocation; a declared length outside 0–1024 is now rejected instead of attempted.<br><br>Not changed: the HMAC key is still derived from the same key material as the cipher. Separating them<br>would change the MAC written into the message and so could not be read by earlier versions; that is<br>tracked separately. | 未調査 |  |
| C423 | 4.22.1→4.22.2 | パッチ | 高 | 削除 | camel-aws2-s3 | camel-aws2-s3 - a listed object that cannot be fetched is skipped | pom/gradle の依存、URIスキーム(例: xxx:)、import、DSL要素を grep。代替先が記載されていれば置換計画を立てる | camel-aws2-s3, DEBUG, WARN, bridgeErrorHandler=true, backoffErrorThreshold, inProgressRepository, fileName | When the consumer lists the bucket, a failure to get one of the listed objects (or to download its content) no longer fails the poll, as long as another object of that listing could be got: the object is skipped, the other listed objects are consumed in that poll, and the skipped object is tried again by a later poll. An object that no longer exists (for example deleted by another consumer after the listing) is skipped with a log line at `DEBUG`. Any other failure is given to the exception handl |  | When the consumer lists the bucket, a failure to get one of the listed objects (or to download its content) no longer<br>fails the poll, as long as another object of that listing could be got: the object is skipped, the other listed<br>objects are consumed in that poll, and the skipped object is tried again by a later poll. An object that no longer<br>exists (for example deleted by another consumer after the listing) is skipped with a log line at `DEBUG`. Any other<br>failure is given to the exception handler of the consumer, with the key in the message: by default that is a `WARN`<br>with the stack trace, and with `bridgeErrorHandler=true` the route's error handler gets it. This happens at every poll<br>that lists an object that can never be read (for example archived, or access denied), until it can be read or is<br>removed from the bucket. Such a poll is a successful poll, so it does not count for `backoffErrorThreshold`.<br><br>The poll still fails, as before, when none of the listed objects could be got and at least one get failed with an<br>error other than that the object no longer exists (for example expired credentials, no permission to get objects,<br>throttling): the failure of the first object is then the failure of the poll, and `backoffErrorThreshold` applies.<br>In both cases the objects are no longer kept in the `inProgressRepository`; before, the object (or a new object with<br>the same key) was skipped by all later polls until the endpoint was restarted. With the `fileName` option, a failed<br>get still fails the poll. | 未調査 |  |
| C424 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-milo | camel-milo - the OPC UA client validates the server certificate | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-milo, None, milo-client, milo-browse, trustListDirectory, trusted/certs, rejected/certs, Bad_CertificateRevocationUnknown, trusted/crl, issuer/crl, certificateValidator, WARN, IllegalStateException: No connected, Failed to connect, because a certificate or security check failed | When the endpoint it selects uses a security policy other than `None`, the `milo-client` and `milo-browse` components now validate the certificate of the OPC UA server. Before, any server certificate was accepted, and no option allowed to validate it. Configure the trusted certificates with the new `trustListDirectory` option: put the certificate of the server, or of the CA that issued it, in the `trusted/certs` directory of the trust list. A server certificate that does not chain up to a truste | あり | When the endpoint it selects uses a security policy other than `None`, the `milo-client` and `milo-browse` components<br>now validate the certificate of the OPC UA server. Before, any server certificate was accepted, and no option allowed<br>to validate it.<br><br>Configure the trusted certificates with the new `trustListDirectory` option: put the certificate of the server, or of<br>the CA that issued it, in the `trusted/certs` directory of the trust list. A server certificate that does not chain up<br>to a trusted certificate is written to `rejected/certs`, from where it can be moved to `trusted/certs` once it has been<br>checked. The trust list also refuses a server certificate outside its validity period, revoked by a revocation list of<br>the trust list, or whose application URI differs from the one of the server. A server certificate issued by a CA is<br>refused with `Bad_CertificateRevocationUnknown` when the trust list holds no revocation list of that CA: add the CRL of<br>the CA (an empty one is enough) to `trusted/crl` or `issuer/crl`. A custom validator can be configured with the new<br>`certificateValidator` option instead.<br><br>With neither option, the client does not connect to such an endpoint. It logs a `WARN` message<br>`Failed to connect: The certificate of the OPC UA server cannot be validated`, followed by the endpoint and its<br>security policy, and tries again every 10 seconds. A producer fails with `IllegalStateException: No connected`, caused<br>by the same message. A server certificate refused by the trust list or by a `certificateValidator` is logged at `WARN`<br>as `Failed to connect, because a certificate or security check failed`. To restore the previous behaviour, set the new<br>`trustAllCertificates` option to `true`. This is insecure: the client then does not authenticate the server.<br><br>The certificate that the user name and password are encrypted with is checked by the same validator. Endpoints that<br>use the security policy `None` are not affected. | 未調査 |  |
| C425 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-platform-http-main | camel-platform-http-main - management server settings on a shared port | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-platform-http-main, camel.server.enabled=true, camel.management.enabled=true, camel.management.host, camel.management.path, camel.management.useGlobalSslContextParameters=true, camel.management.authenticationEnabled=true, camel.management.port, /* | When the HTTP server (`camel.server.enabled=true`) and the HTTP management server (`camel.management.enabled=true`) have the same port (both default to 8080), the HTTP server serves the management endpoints. It cannot apply these options of the management server, which were ignored without notice: * `camel.management.host`, when set to another host than the one of the HTTP server * `camel.management.path`, when set to another path than the one of the HTTP server * `camel.management.useGlobalSslC | あり | When the HTTP server (`camel.server.enabled=true`) and the HTTP management server (`camel.management.enabled=true`)<br>have the same port (both default to 8080), the HTTP server serves the management endpoints. It cannot apply these<br>options of the management server, which were ignored without notice:<br><br>* `camel.management.host`, when set to another host than the one of the HTTP server<br>* `camel.management.path`, when set to another path than the one of the HTTP server<br>* `camel.management.useGlobalSslContextParameters=true`, when the HTTP server does not use the global SSL configuration<br>* `camel.management.authenticationEnabled=true`, with the basic or JWT authentication options<br><br>Camel now fails to start when the management server shares the port and one of them is configured, with a message<br>that lists them. Set `camel.management.port` to another port, so that the management server runs a server of its own<br>and applies them. To keep a single port, remove them and configure the HTTP server instead: for example,<br>authentication configured on the HTTP server for `/*` also applies to the management endpoints. | 未調査 |  |
| C426 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-elasticsearch | camel-elasticsearch - the credentials are only sent to the nodes of the cluster | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-elasticsearch, user, password, hostAddresses, enableSniffer, client | The `user` and `password` are now offered only to the nodes the client talks to: the hosts of `hostAddresses` and, when `enableSniffer` is set, the nodes the sniffer finds, matching the scheme, host and port. Previously they were registered for any host. A request to another host, including the host of a node with another scheme or port, is now sent without them. A client set with the `client` option is not changed. | あり | The `user` and `password` are now offered only to the nodes the client talks to: the hosts of `hostAddresses` and,<br>when `enableSniffer` is set, the nodes the sniffer finds, matching the scheme, host and port. Previously they were<br>registered for any host. A request to another host, including the host of a node with another scheme or port, is now<br>sent without them. A client set with the `client` option is not changed. | 未調査 |  |
| C427 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-thrift | camel-thrift - SSL/TLS settings of the consumer, and errors sent to the client | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-thrift, negotiationType=SSL, synchronous=false, synchronous=true, SASL, PLAINTEXT, sslParameters, serverParameters.clientAuthentication=REQUIRE, keyPassword, muteException, TApplicationException, INTERNAL_ERROR, muteException=false | * A consumer configured with `negotiationType=SSL` and the default `synchronous=false` now fails to start. It used to start a server without SSL/TLS. SSL/TLS requires `synchronous=true`, as on the producer. * The `SASL` negotiation type, which is not implemented, now makes the producer and the consumer fail to start. They used to behave as with `PLAINTEXT`. * The SSL/TLS consumer now creates its server socket from the SSL context of `sslParameters`, so all of its settings apply, including the tr | あり | * A consumer configured with `negotiationType=SSL` and the default `synchronous=false` now fails to start. It used to<br>start a server without SSL/TLS. SSL/TLS requires `synchronous=true`, as on the producer.<br>* The `SASL` negotiation type, which is not implemented, now makes the producer and the consumer fail to start. They<br>used to behave as with `PLAINTEXT`.<br>* The SSL/TLS consumer now creates its server socket from the SSL context of `sslParameters`, so all of its settings<br>apply, including the trust managers and the server parameters. For example, `serverParameters.clientAuthentication=REQUIRE`<br>now requires a client certificate. Before, the consumer only used the key store, the protocol and the cipher suites,<br>and never asked for a client certificate. The key managers are required, and as in the other components the key is<br>read with their `keyPassword`: set it when the key is protected by a password. Before, the consumer read the key with<br>the password of the key store.<br>* A new `muteException` consumer option, enabled by default, sends a generic `TApplicationException` of type<br>`INTERNAL_ERROR` ("Internal error processing <method>") to the client instead of an exception that the Thrift method<br>does not declare. Before, the asynchronous consumer sent the message of the exception. An exception declared in the<br>IDL is still sent as it is. Set `muteException=false` to send the exception as before. | 未調査 |  |
| C428 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-elasticsearch-rest-client | camel-elasticsearch-rest-client - the credentials are only sent to the nodes of the cluster | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-elasticsearch-rest-client, user, password, hostAddressesList, enableSniffer, restClient | The `user` and `password` are now offered only to the nodes the client talks to: the hosts of `hostAddressesList` and, when `enableSniffer` is set, the nodes the sniffer finds, matching the scheme, host and port. Previously they were registered for any host. A request to another host, including the host of a node with another scheme or port, is now sent without them. A client set with the `restClient` option is not changed. | あり | The `user` and `password` are now offered only to the nodes the client talks to: the hosts of `hostAddressesList` and,<br>when `enableSniffer` is set, the nodes the sniffer finds, matching the scheme, host and port. Previously they were<br>registered for any host. A request to another host, including the host of a node with another scheme or port, is now<br>sent without them. A client set with the `restClient` option is not changed. | 未調査 |  |
| C429 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-smooks | camel-smooks - allowExternalEntities applies to Smooks Source bodies and to a reader declared without a class | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-smooks, SmooksProcessor, Source, org.smooks.io.source.StringSource, ReaderSource, StreamSource, ByteSource, URLSource, allowExternalEntities, true, DOMSource, JavaSource, <reader>, class | The Smooks component and `SmooksProcessor` now parse a message body that is already a Smooks `Source` (`org.smooks.io.source.StringSource`, `ReaderSource`, `StreamSource`, `ByteSource` or `URLSource`) with the same XML reader settings as the other message bodies, so external entities in it are only resolved when `allowExternalEntities` is `true`. Before, such a body was handed to Smooks as it was. The bytes of a `StreamSource`, `ByteSource` or `URLSource` are decoded with the exchange charset, o | あり | The Smooks component and `SmooksProcessor` now parse a message body that is already a Smooks `Source`<br>(`org.smooks.io.source.StringSource`, `ReaderSource`, `StreamSource`, `ByteSource` or `URLSource`) with the same XML<br>reader settings as the other message bodies, so external entities in it are only resolved when `allowExternalEntities`<br>is `true`. Before, such a body was handed to Smooks as it was. The bytes of a `StreamSource`, `ByteSource` or<br>`URLSource` are decoded with the exchange charset, or UTF-8, as before. These bodies are now parsed into a DOM before<br>Smooks processes them, which uses more memory for very large inputs. `DOMSource` and `JavaSource` bodies are unchanged.<br><br>A Smooks configuration whose `<reader>` declares no `class` only sets handlers, features or parameters of the default<br>XML reader. The Smooks component, `SmooksProcessor` and the Smooks data format now apply `allowExternalEntities` to<br>such a configuration as they do to a configuration without a `<reader>`, so the handlers and features of that reader no<br>longer take part in parsing the XML unless `allowExternalEntities` is `true`. Configurations that declare a reader<br>class, such as EDI, CSV, JSON, DFDL or a custom reader, are unchanged.<br><br>A document with a document type declaration (`<!DOCTYPE ...>`) is now processed with these settings for every body<br>type, `String`, `byte[]` and `InputStream` bodies included, which failed before: the entities of its internal subset are<br>expanded, and the declaration itself is not passed on to Smooks.<br><br>Set `allowExternalEntities=true` on the endpoint or on the data format for documents that rely on external entities or<br>an external DTD. | 未調査 |  |
| C430 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-ssh | camel-ssh - known_hosts entries are matched as in OpenSSH | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-ssh, knownHostsResource, known_hosts, host, [host]:port, db.example.com, [db.example.com]:2222, HostName, ::1, @revoked, @cert-authority, failOnUnknownHost | When `knownHostsResource` is set, the entries of the `known_hosts` file are now matched as OpenSSH matches them, against the host name or address the client connects to, written `host` for port 22 and `[host]:port` for another port: * A host pattern must match that name as a whole. An entry for another host whose name or address contains the configured one is no longer used. * A pattern such as `db.example.com` only applies to port 22. A server on another port needs an entry such as `[db.example | あり | When `knownHostsResource` is set, the entries of the `known_hosts` file are now matched as OpenSSH<br>matches them, against the host name or address the client connects to, written `host` for port 22 and<br>`[host]:port` for another port:<br><br>* A host pattern must match that name as a whole. An entry for another host whose name or address<br>contains the configured one is no longer used.<br>* A pattern such as `db.example.com` only applies to port 22. A server on another port needs an entry<br>such as `[db.example.com]:2222`, or a pattern that matches that form, such as `*`.<br>* The host is used as it is written: the host configured on the endpoint, or the `HostName` that<br>`~/.ssh/config` gives for it. An endpoint configured with a host name no longer uses entries listed<br>only under its address, an endpoint configured with an address no longer uses entries listed under the<br>name that a reverse lookup of the address returns, and an IPv6 address such as `::1` is matched as<br>written instead of in its expanded form.<br>* Every entry of the host is considered, so a host can be listed with several keys. Wildcard, negated<br>and hashed patterns, comments and `@revoked` entries are supported. `@cert-authority` entries are<br>ignored.<br>* A `known_hosts` resource that cannot be read, or that has a line that cannot be read (for example an<br>unknown `@` marker, a missing key, or a key that is not valid base64), now makes every connection fail,<br>whatever the value of `failOnUnknownHost`. Previously such a resource was treated as having no entry,<br>and such a line was skipped.<br><br>As before, a server whose host has entries without a marker is rejected when it presents a key that<br>none of them lists, whatever the value of `failOnUnknownHost`, which only applies to a host without<br>such an entry: `@revoked` and `@cert-authority` entries do not list a host.<br>Check that the `known_hosts` file has an entry for the host name or address, and the port, that each<br>endpoint is configured with. | 未調査 |  |
| C431 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-a2a | camel-a2a - caller profile and task owner | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-a2a, CamelA2AUserProfile, {"scheme": "apiKey"}, sub, username, client_id, azp, CamelOAuthTokenValidationResult | * When a security requirement of the agent card combines several schemes, such as an API key and an OAuth token, the caller profile (`CamelA2AUserProfile`) is now the one of the token, whatever the order of the schemes. Before, it was the profile of the first scheme, so a requirement that listed the API key first only gave `{"scheme": "apiKey"}` to the route, and the tasks belonged to the API key. * A token without a `sub` claim is now identified by the `username` that a token introspection resp |  | * When a security requirement of the agent card combines several schemes, such as an API key and an OAuth token, the<br>caller profile (`CamelA2AUserProfile`) is now the one of the token, whatever the order of the schemes. Before, it was<br>the profile of the first scheme, so a requirement that listed the API key first only gave `{"scheme": "apiKey"}` to<br>the route, and the tasks belonged to the API key.<br>* A token without a `sub` claim is now identified by the `username` that a token introspection response gives, else by<br>its `client_id` or `azp` claim (such as a client credentials token), so the tasks of different users and clients are<br>kept apart. A valid token that has none of these claims is now rejected with HTTP 401.<br>* The `CamelOAuthTokenValidationResult` exchange property is now set on the exchange that the route processes, as<br>documented. Before, it was only set on the incoming HTTP exchange. | 未調査 |  |
| C432 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 高 | セキュリティ強化(挙動変更) | camel-opensearch | camel-opensearch - the credentials are only sent to the nodes of the cluster | 該当コンポーネントを使用しているか grep。使用していれば、拒否される入力・必要な追加オプションがないか原文で確認し、結合テストで検証 | camel-opensearch, user, password, hostAddresses, enableSniffer, client, openSearchClient | The `user` and `password` are now offered only to the nodes the client talks to: the hosts of `hostAddresses` and, when `enableSniffer` is set, the nodes the sniffer finds, matching the scheme, host and port. Every node of a multi-host cluster still receives them. Previously they were registered for any host. A request to another host, including the host of a node with another scheme or port, is now sent without them. A client set with the `client` or `openSearchClient` option is not changed. | あり | The `user` and `password` are now offered only to the nodes the client talks to: the hosts of `hostAddresses` and,<br>when `enableSniffer` is set, the nodes the sniffer finds, matching the scheme, host and port. Every node of a<br>multi-host cluster still receives them. Previously they were registered for any host. A request to another host,<br>including the host of a node with another scheme or port, is now sent without them. A client set with the `client` or<br>`openSearchClient` option is not changed. | 未調査 |  |
| C433 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-undertow | camel-undertow - the producer refuses a request target or header value with control characters | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-undertow, 0xFF, IllegalArgumentException, CamelHttpPath, CamelHttpQuery | The undertow producer writes the path, query and header values of the outgoing request to the socket one character at a time, without validating them. A carriage return or line feed therefore broke the request into further lines, and a character above `0xFF` was written as a single, different byte (for example `U+010A` became a line feed). The producer now refuses to send a request path, query or header value that contains a control character or a character above `0xFF`, and fails the exchange w | あり | The undertow producer writes the path, query and header values of the outgoing request to the socket one character at<br>a time, without validating them. A carriage return or line feed therefore broke the request into further lines, and a<br>character above `0xFF` was written as a single, different byte (for example `U+010A` became a line feed). The producer<br>now refuses to send a request path, query or header value that contains a control character or a character above<br>`0xFF`, and fails the exchange with an `IllegalArgumentException` instead. A space and a tab, which do not change the<br>framing, are still allowed. Routes that put a percent-encoded control character (such as `%0D%0A`) into the<br>`CamelHttpPath` or `CamelHttpQuery` header, which the producer decodes before building the request, are the ones most<br>likely to be affected. | 未調査 |  |
| C434 | 4.22.2→4.22.3 | パッチ | 中 | 挙動変更 | camel-core | camel-core - pollEnrich: the body is null after a timeout also for a message that creates its body on demand | 該当コンポーネント/EIPの使用箇所を grep し、原文の挙動差分が自システムに影響するか確認 | camel-core, pollEnrich, poll, aggregationStrategy, null, variableReceive, GenericFileMessage, JmsMessage | When `pollEnrich` (or `poll`) times out and no `aggregationStrategy` is configured, the body is set to `null`, and with `variableReceive` the variable is `null`. For a message that creates its body on demand, the `null` did not stick: the next read created the body again. The message of a file consumer creates its body from its file, so after a timeout the body, or the variable of `variableReceive`, was the file of the incoming exchange instead of `null`. The messages of the JMS, sjms, mail, HTT | あり | When `pollEnrich` (or `poll`) times out and no `aggregationStrategy` is configured, the body is set to `null`, and with<br>`variableReceive` the variable is `null`. For a message that creates its body on demand, the `null` did not stick: the<br>next read created the body again. The message of a file consumer creates its body from its file, so after a timeout<br>the body, or the variable of `variableReceive`, was the file of the incoming exchange instead of `null`. The messages<br>of the JMS, sjms, mail, HTTP, XMPP, SMPP, SNMP and Spring WS consumers create their body on demand as well, so there it<br>was the payload of the consumer again.<br><br>The body, or the variable, is now `null` after a timeout for these consumers too. A route that read the incoming file<br>or payload from the body after a timed out `pollEnrich` must keep it before the `pollEnrich` instead, for example with<br>`variableReceive`, which leaves the body as it was. To keep the body empty, the message is replaced by a plain message<br>with the same message id, headers and attachments, so after a timeout it is no longer of the message type of the<br>consumer (such as `GenericFileMessage` or `JmsMessage`). | 未調査 |  |

